`STATUS=OK rows=12 findings=0 unknown=0`, `GPC` prints `PASS`, `RCC` prints its `OK:` line, `G diff --numstat HEAD -- AGENTS.md` prints `1`, `1` and `AGENTS.md`, `sed -n 65p AGENTS.md | wc -c` prints 205, `sed -n 35p $CUR | rg -c -- '--json - --format json'` prints 1 and `comm -23 <(G show HEAD:$AMM | jq -r '.derived.history[].sha256' | sort) <(jq -r '.derived.history[].sha256' $AMM | sort)` prints nothing.\n104: \n105: ### Wave 3\n106: - [ ] T016 [C] Regenerate every runtime copy of the commands and the agents (`.claude/commands`, `.cursor/commands`, `.codex/prompts`, `.pi/prompts`, `.dsh/prompts`, `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents`, `.dsh/agents`). Run `node $MS`, then the three `sync-prompts` and the three `sync-agents` generators of `PSY` and `ASY` without `--check`. Verify: `SRM` prints `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude 44/44, cursor 44/44` and `PASS: 256 mirrors across 10 trees are in sync.`, `PSY` prints `45` three times, `ASY` prints `11` three times, `AMSC` is in sync, `readlink .claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` prints `../../../.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `readlink .cursor/commands/create-sk-skill.md` prints `../../.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `ls .codex/prompts/create-sk-skill.md .pi/prompts/create-sk-skill.md .dsh/prompts/create-sk-skill.md` lists three files, `find .claude/commands .cursor/commands .codex/prompts .pi/prompts .dsh/prompts \\( -iname skill.md -o -name create-skill.md \\)` prints nothing and `readlink .claude/skills` prints `../.skilled/skills`.\n107: - [ ] T017 [C] Rebuild the advisor, restart the worktree's daemon and re-embed (`$ADV/dist`, the advisor database). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, restart the advisor daemon this worktree serves, then `CLI skill_graph_scan --trusted --format text`. Verify: the build exits 0, `TC` exits 0, `rg -c 'appear' $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.js` prints at least 1, `rg -c 'create:sk-skill' $ADV/dist/runtime/lib/command-attach.js` prints at least 1 and the scan prints its status with no error. When Ollama does not answer, mark this task `[B]` and start nothing.\n108: - [ ] T018 [C] Read the fixture floors and take the real capture before lane D (`$SP/real-before-d.json`). Run `FLOOR` without `--write`, then `REAL` into `$SP/real-before-d.json` and read it. Verify: `FLOOR` prints typed recall of 24 of 44 or more, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, typed delivery `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` or a `combined` of 44, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`. The `REAL` read prints typed 24 of 44 or more, false offers `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` in both columns and `[false,false,false]`, and its tune and holdout counts are written into `$SP/before.txt` as the lane D before line, holdout as a count only.\n109: \n110: ### Wave 4\n111: - [ ] T019 [P] Lane D. Add intent phrases to the five scored commands that have no recommendation (`RTS`, `SSK` and the `DER` outputs). Take the phrases in `added` for `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search` from `LIN`, and leave `/create:skill-parent` out. Before adding them, read the prompts of `cmd-doctor-install-plain-tune-01`, `cmd-doctor-setup-plain-tune-01`, `cmd-doctor-speckit-plain-tune-01`, `cmd-doctor-update-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-search-plain-tune-01` from `CORPUS` by id, each after checking that its `split` is `tune`. Compare each phrase with its command's tune prompt after lowercasing and collapsing spaces, and rewrite any phrase that equals that prompt or holds it whole as a paraphrase that keeps the intent words and changes the rest, because a phrase copied from a tune prompt counts as gain only on tune. Never read or compare a holdout row. Add the four doctor commands' phrases to `trigger_phrases` of their routes in `RTS` and the search phrases to `userIntent.ownedSignals` of `/speckit:search` in `SSK`, then run `DER`. Verify: a script that compares every added phrase with the five tune prompts on the same normalized text prints `0`, `RV` holds `32 routes validated`, `DPR` prints `STATUS=OK` with `phrases=` higher than `$SP/before.txt` by the number of doctor phrases added, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `jq empty $SSK` passes and `TC` exits 0.\n112: \n113: ### Wave 5\n114: - [ ] T020 [C] Rebuild, restart, re-embed and take the real capture after lane D (`$ADV/dist`, the advisor database, `$SP/real-after-d.json`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, restart the daemon, run `CLI skill_graph_scan --trusted --format text`, then `REAL` into `$SP/real-after-d.json` and read it. Verify: the build exits 0, the scan prints no error, typed reads 24 of 44 or more, false offers read `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` in both columns, the floor rows print `[false,false,false]` and the holdout count is at least 2 above the lane D before line from T018. Record the tune counts as built in, not as gain. A smaller holdout gain is reported as measured, and no phrase changes after this count is read.\n115: \n116: ### Wave 6\n117: - [ ] T021 [P] Recapture the fixture baseline and check the scorer eval (`BASE`, and `$RA/scorer-eval-baseline.json` only when its values move). Run `node $CAP --write`, `FLOOR` and `EVAL`. When `EVAL` differs from the committed baseline and still holds the floor, recapture it with `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs --write` as its header documents and run `V tests/parity/scorer-eval-baseline-ratchet.vitest.ts tests/parity/scorer-eval-baseline-capture-date.vitest.ts`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints typed recall of 24 of 44 or more, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, a typed delivery `combined` of 44 of 44, a plain tune `combined` of 23 or more and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq -c '.rows[\"cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01\"].offered, .rows[\"cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01\"].offered' $BASE` prints `true` and `false`, `jq -r '.commands | keys[]' $BASE | rg -cx '/create:sk-skill'` prints 1, `OLD $BASE` prints nothing, `SLICE` reports 0 failed and `EVAL` prints at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5.\n118: \n119: ### Wave 7\n120: - [ ] T022 [C] Observe Claude's command folder without a model session (`$SP/claude-observed.txt`). Run `SRM`, `ls .claude/commands/create` and `find .claude/commands -iname skill.md | wc -l`. Verify: `SRM` prints `visibility claude 44/44`, the listing holds 13 entries with `sk-skill.md` among them and the count prints 0. These three facts are the proof a coordinator can take. Claude's own listing is T023's.\n121: - [ ] T023 [C] Ask the operator for one live Claude Code listing of the regenerated tree (`$SP/claude-listing.txt`). It needs a model session, so it is the operator's to run and confirm. Write the expected names with `(cd .claude/commands && find . -name '*.md' -not -name 'local-*' | sed -e 's|^\\./||' -e 's|\\.md$||' -e 's|/|:|') | sort > $SP/claude-expected.txt`. In a directory from `mktemp -d` outside any repository, copy the tree with `cp -RL .claude/commands <tmp>/x/.claude/commands`, start Claude Code once in `<tmp>/x` with the prompt \"List the names of every entry your Skill tool offers, one per line, and nothing else.\", save the answer to `$SP/claude-listing.txt` and delete the temp directory. Verify: `wc -l < $SP/claude-expected.txt` prints 44 and `comm -23 $SP/claude-expected.txt <(sed -E 's/^[-*/ ]+//' $SP/claude-listing.txt | sort -u)` prints nothing, so `create:sk-skill` and the twelve other `create:*` names are listed. Until the operator runs it, this task stays open and REQ-012 rests on T022.\n122: - [ ] T024 [C] Read the live doctor brief and the CLI answer for the two doctor rows (`$SP/doctor-live.txt`). For each of `cmd-doctor-mcp-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-doctor-skill-advisor-plain-tune-01`, build the hook payload with `jq -c --arg cwd \"$PWD\" 'select(.id == \"<id>\") | if .split == \"tune\" then {prompt, cwd: $cwd, hook_event_name: \"UserPromptSubmit\", session_id: \"doctor-helper-check\"} else error(\"not a tune row\") end' $CORPUS`, pipe it into `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node $HOOK` and keep `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. Then build `{prompt}` the same way, pipe it into `CLI advisor_recommend --json - --format json` and keep `jq -c '.data.recommendations[] | select(.skillId == \"command-doctor-helper\") | [.command, .policy]'`. Write each result beside its row id, never the prompt. Verify: the mcp brief holds a line starting `Also: /doctor:helper`, the mcp CLI line prints `[\"/doctor:helper\",\"run\"]`, the skill-advisor brief holds no `/doctor:` and its CLI line prints nothing.\n123: - [ ] T025 [C] Run the brief-cost script once and prove the health log is untouched (`$SP/brief-cost-run.txt`). Record `find \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics\" -type f -exec wc -l {} +`, run `node $MBC --rows cmd-create-agent-typed-01` and record its exit code and its first line, then record the same `find` again. Verify: the two `find` outputs are identical, and the script either exits 0 with one live row or exits 2 with `degraded_brief`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n124: \n125: ### Wave 8\n126: - [ ] T026 Write the changelog entry for the breaking rename at `v2.10.0.0`, the version the operator chose in Q3 (the `sk-doc` changelog entry and the `version` fields of `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md`, `hub-router.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `description.json`). Write the entry through the `sk-create-changelog` workflow as `v2.10.0.0`, a minor bump whose text calls out the break, and set the four version fields to `2.10.0.0`. Its first line of substance says `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, and why. Edit no existing entry. Verify: `G status --short -- '*/changelog/*'` lists only the new entry, `G diff --quiet HEAD -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog .skilled/changelog` exits 0 and `PSC` holds `all hard invariants passed, 0 warnings`.\n127: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n132: ## Phase 3: Verification\n133: \n134: - [ ] T027 [C] Run every floor and check (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `DRV`, `SRM`, `NMST`, `PSY`, `ASY`, `AMSC`, `AMC`, `MAN`, `GPC`, `RCC`, `CRS`, `PSC`, `CCM`, `RV` and `DPR`, and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` holds every floor in REQ-007, `EVAL` prints at least `[160,50,21,5]` with the fourth value no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []`, `SRM` prints `visibility claude 44/44, cursor 44/44`, `NMST` reports `fail 0`, `PSY`, `ASY` and `AMSC` pass, `AMC`, `MAN`, `GPC` and `RCC` pass, `CRS` prints both lines, `PSC` holds `all hard invariants passed`, `CCM` prints `STATUS=OK`, `RV` holds `32 routes validated` and `DPR` starts `STATUS=OK`.\n135: - [ ] T028 [C] Check the rename's end state and the boundaries. Verify: `OLD` prints exactly the nine `KEPT` files, `rg -l -F 'create:sk-skill' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md .skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json $ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` lists all three, `G diff --quiet HEAD -- .claude/skills .skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md $ADV/lib/render.ts` exits 0, every `KEPT` file is unchanged by `G diff --quiet HEAD --`, `G diff --stat HEAD -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `G diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|[Pp]hase [0-9]|[Rr]ank [0-9]|R4-P2)\"` prints nothing, `G diff --numstat HEAD -- AGENTS.md` prints `1`, `1` and `AGENTS.md`, and `G status --short -- .skilled .claude .cursor .codex .pi .dsh AGENTS.md README.md CONTRIBUTING.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n136: - [ ] T029 [C] Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n137: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n142: ## Completion Criteria\n143: \n144: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`, with T023 allowed open only while it waits on the operator\n145: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n146: - [ ] `OLD` lists only the nine `KEPT` files, `SRM` prints `visibility claude 44/44`, `BASE` holds every floor, the real holdout count rose by at least 2 in T020 and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n147: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n152: ## Cross-References\n153: \n154: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n155: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n156: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n157: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md` and `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-4.md`\n158: - **Review**: `../review/review-report.md`\n159: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n160: \n161: ---\n162: \n163: ## Verification Checklist\n164: \n165: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n166: ## Verification Protocol\n167: \n168: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n169: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n170: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n171: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n172: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n173: \n174: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n175: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n176: \n177: ---\n178: \n179: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n180: ## Pre-Implementation\n181: \n182: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The base is clean and phase 015 is committed (T001). Evidence: the T001 verify lines.\n183: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `scratch/before.txt` and match `spec.md` section 2 (T002). Evidence: the T002 verify lines.\n184: - [ ] CHK-003 [P0] The command file moved with its history (T003). Evidence: the `R` status line.\n185: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n186: \n187: ---\n188: \n189: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n190: ## Code Quality\n191: \n192: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `MS`, `MBC` and the schema helper. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and the T004, T007 and T013 verifies.\n193: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No added code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a rank id or a finding id (T028). Evidence: the T028 label scan prints nothing.\n194: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] Every generated file was written by its generator, and every generator check passes (T014, T015, T016, T019, T021). Evidence: `DRV`, `SRM`, `PSY`, `ASY`, `MAN`, `GPC` and `SLICE`.\n195: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] `AGENTS.md` changes on line 65 only (T015, T028). Evidence: the `numstat` line reads `1`, `1`.\n196: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n201: ## Testing Checklist\n202: \n203: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T021, T027). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`.\n204: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The old-name scan lists only the nine kept files (T028). Evidence: the `OLD` output.\n205: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The mirror check reads 44 of 44 with no allowlist and fails on a capitalised `SKILL.md` (T004, T016). Evidence: `NMST` and the `SRM` line.\n206: - [ ] CHK-023 [P0] The tests written first failed before their change and pass after it (T004, T012, T013). Evidence: `fail 2`, `fail 1` and `1 failed` before, 0 after.\n207: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] The real holdout count rose by at least 2 with every real floor held (T018, T020). Evidence: `$SP/real-before-d.json` and `$SP/real-after-d.json`.\n208: - [ ] CHK-025 [P1] The live brief and the CLI name `/doctor:helper` on the mcp tune row and on no other doctor row checked (T024). Evidence: `$SP/doctor-live.txt`.\n209: - [ ] CHK-026 [P1] Claude's folder holds no `skill.md` in any capitalisation, and the operator's listing names all 44 (T022, T023). Evidence: `$SP/claude-observed.txt` and `$SP/claude-listing.txt`.\n210: - [ ] CHK-027 [P1] A cost run leaves the shared health log unchanged (T025). Evidence: `$SP/brief-cost-run.txt`.\n211: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n212: \n213: ---\n214: \n215: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n216: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n217: \n218: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each item has a class: the rename `cross-consumer` (55 files and five runtimes), the collapse check `class-of-bug` (any folder, any capitalisation), the doctor cue `instance-only`, the Gate 2 line `cross-consumer` (three copies), the intent phrases `matrix/evidence` (fixture and real captures) and the cost run `instance-only`. Evidence: the classes match the affected surfaces in `plan.md`.\n219: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: the `OLD` scan covers every spelling of the old name across hidden runtime trees, and `rg -n \"skill\\.md\" $MS` lists only the case-free comparisons. Evidence: the two outputs.\n220: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every consumer of a changed output is in the `plan.md` addendum. Evidence: the generator list and the `OLD` scan name no file outside it.\n221: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` each have a case in T004, T011, T018, T020 or an existing test. Evidence: the case names and the two real captures.\n222: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] `VALL` runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset, and the T024 hook run unsets it too. Evidence: the T027 and T024 commands.\n223: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name it.\n224: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n225: \n226: ---\n227: \n228: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n229: ## Security\n230: \n231: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text or opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. Evidence: the holdout corpus row changed by a count-only `sed` in T010, every capture publishes holdout as counts, and T011, T019 and T024 read tune rows by id after checking the split.\n232: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No worker starts a model session, a daemon or Ollama, moves a file with git or writes under the home folder. Evidence: T003, T016, T017, T018, T020 and T022 to T025 are coordinator tasks, and T023 is the operator's.\n233: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The documented direct call sends the prompt on stdin (T015). Evidence: `sed -n 65p AGENTS.md` and the T012 case.\n234: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n235: \n236: ---\n237: \n238: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n239: ## Documentation\n240: \n241: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers. Evidence: 55 files to nine, 32 of 44 to 44 of 44, `offered` false to true, a 188-byte line to a 204-byte line and the holdout delta read the same in each.\n242: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The mirror README, the hook guide, the root docs and the changelog entry match the code (T004, T008, T009, T026). Evidence: their verify commands print what they say.\n243: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n244: \n245: ---\n246: \n247: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n248: ## File Organization\n249: \n250: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Every measurement lives in `scratch/` and no probe script is left in the tree. Evidence: `ls scratch` lists the files the tasks name.\n251: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] No file outside the tasks' list changed (T028). Evidence: the T028 status line.\n252: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n253: \n254: ---\n255: \n256: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n257: ## Verification Summary\n258: \n259: | Category | Total | Verified |\n260: |----------|-------|----------|\n261: | P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n262: | P1 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n263: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n264: \n265: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n266: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582774129,"end":1794582774677}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794582777051,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"id":"prt_1d5780cdb001LXQwFXs17MPAFZ","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d577e3fe001wUd9dsuRyEc6Jl","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":17196,"output":105,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":384,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794582781676,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"id":"prt_1d5781eec001w7O95s4B6Mm33n","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5780ce7001Frrw7haNt4XeUX","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582791139,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d57840d2002HMwC8opQ6lwAn0","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5780ce7001Frrw7haNt4XeUX","type":"tool","id":"call_1d0c1eed0a854d588a4dd430","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/README.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/README.txt, lines 1-215\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Create Commands\"\n3: description: \"Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, docs, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"create command\"\n6:   - \"scaffold component\"\n7:   - \"create agent\"\n8:   - \"create skill\"\n9:   - \"create readme\"\n10:   - \"create feature catalog\"\n11:   - \"create testing playbook\"\n12:   - \"create changelog\"\n13:   - \"create chart\"\n14:   - \"create diagram\"\n15:   - \"create diff\"\n16:   - \"create repo rule\"\n17:   - \"apply human voice\"\n18: ---\n19: \n20: # Create Commands\n21: \n22: > Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, charts, diagrams, diff reports and repo rules with proper templates and validation.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n27: \n28: The `create` command group scaffolds OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, and standalone visual and prose artifacts. All commands follow a structured YAML workflow and support `:auto` (no approval prompts) and `:confirm` (pause at each step) execution modes.\n29: \n30: The table in section 3 lists every command in this folder. When a command file is added here, add its row there too; a missing row is the failure mode this index has hit before.\n31: \n32: All shipped `create` commands run Phase 0 (@markdown agent self-verification).\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. PURPOSE\n37: \n38: Use this index to understand which `/create:*` command owns a given scaffolding workflow, which argument shape it expects, and which package contract or artifact family it generates.\n39: \n40: This document is a routing and reference surface only. Run the command entrypoint itself for execution, setup prompting, and YAML workflow dispatch.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. COMMANDS\n45: | Command | Invocation | Description |\n46: |---------|------------|-------------|\n47: | **agent** | `/create:agent <agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, and behavioral rules |\n48: | **benchmark** | `/create:benchmark <skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> [create\\|update] --family=<family> [--benchmark-id <id>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages |\n49: | **changelog** | `/create:changelog <spec-folder-or-component> [--bump <major\\|minor\\|patch\\|build\\|auto>] [--release] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a global changelog entry under `.skilled/changelog/` that search can find, with a GitHub release for the `skilled` line when asked |\n50: | **command** | `/create:command <command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or update an OpenCode slash command set with router and `:auto`/`:confirm` workflow assets |\n51: | **diff** | `/create:diff <target-document \\| --before old --after new> [--report out.html] [--view unified\\|side-by-side] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a self-contained before/after document diff report via the create-diff engine |\n52: | **feature-catalog** | `/create:feature-catalog <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or update a rooted `feature-catalog/` package using the shipped `sk-doc` contract |\n53: | **goal** | `/create:goal <packet path> [top-level\\|phase-parent\\|child\\|retrofit\\|phase-add\\|amend] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Author or revise a packet `goal.md` for top-level, phase-parent, child, retrofit, phase-add and amend |\n54: | **manual-testing-playbook** | `/create:manual-testing-playbook <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or update a rooted `manual-testing-playbook/` package using the shipped `sk-doc` contract |\n55: | **readme** | `/create:readme <target> [--type <project\\|component\\|feature\\|skill>] [--output <path>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Folder README creation with `sk-doc` quality standards |\n56: | **repo-rule** | `/create:repo-rule <what the rule should bind> [create\\|revise\\|retire] [--rule <name>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create, revise or retire a repo rule under `repo-rules/`, wired into `REPO RULES.md` |\n57: | **skill** | `/create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Unified skill workflow (full-create, full-update, reference-only, asset-only) |\n58: | **skill-parent** | `/create:skill-parent <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--modes <m1,m2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, `mode-registry.json` source of truth, and a root `ROUTER.md` stage-two control document) |\n59: | **with-human-voice** | `/create:with-human-voice <file or passage> [apply\\|score] [--include-code] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules with a scope gate and a re-scan |\n60: \n61: ### README Types\n62: \n63: The `readme` operation in `/create:readme` accepts a `--type` flag:\n64: \n65: | Type | Use Case |\n66: |------|----------|\n67: | `project` | Root-level project documentation |\n68: | `component` | Reusable module or library |\n69: | `feature` | Specific feature or system |\n70: | `skill` | AI skill supplementary documentation |\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 4. STRUCTURE\n75: \n76: ```\n77: create/\n78: ├── agent.md                      # /create:agent command\n79: ├── benchmark.md                  # /create:benchmark command\n80: ├── changelog.md                  # /create:changelog command\n81: ├── command.md                    # /create:command command\n82: ├── diff.md                       # /create:diff command\n83: ├── feature-catalog.md            # /create:feature-catalog command\n84: ├── goal.md                       # /create:goal command\n85: ├── manual-testing-playbook.md    # /create:manual-testing-playbook command\n86: ├── readme.md                     # /create:readme — folder README command\n87: ├── repo-rule.md                  # /create:repo-rule command\n88: ├── skill.md                      # /create:skill command\n89: ├── skill-parent.md               # /create:skill-parent command\n90: ├── with-human-voice.md           # /create:with-human-voice command\n91: └── assets/                       # One auto YAML, one confirm YAML and one presentation\n92:                                   # contract per command; see the folder itself for the\n93:                                   # live file set rather than a count kept here\n94: ```\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: ## 5. INSTRUCTIONS\n99: \n100: 1. Pick the command family that matches the artifact you need.\n101: 2. Use the canonical command entrypoint, not a deprecated alias.\n102: 3. Supply `:auto` for autonomous execution or `:confirm` for checkpointed execution.\n103: 4. For rooted documentation packages, use the package-specific commands instead of composing the files manually.\n104: 5. If the command performs file modifications, keep it attached to the active spec workflow.\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 6. EXECUTION MODES\n109: \n110: | Mode | Suffix | Behavior |\n111: |------|--------|----------|\n112: | **Auto** | `:auto` | Execute all steps without approval prompts |\n113: | **Confirm** | `:confirm` | Pause at each step and wait for user approval |\n114: \n115: Each mode loads a separate YAML workflow from `assets/` when that command ships YAML assets:\n116: - Auto: `create-<command>-auto.yaml`\n117: - Confirm: `create-<command>-confirm.yaml`\n118: \n119: The `--chained` flag on `/create:skill` doc-only operations indicates parent workflow handoff.\n120: \n121: The documentation-package commands preserve the live `sk-doc` contracts:\n122: - `/create:feature-catalog` produces `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` plus bare descriptive-slug category folders (the root catalog owns display order)\n123: - `/create:manual-testing-playbook` produces `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` plus bare descriptive-slug category folders (the root playbook owns display order) and no sidecar review/ledger files\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: ## 7. USAGE EXAMPLES\n128: \n129: ```bash\n130: # Create a new agent in auto mode\n131: /create:agent my-analyzer \"Code analysis specialist\" :auto\n132: \n133: # Create a README for a specific folder\n134: /create:readme readme .skilled/skills/my-skill --type skill :confirm\n135: \n136: # Create a full skill\n137: /create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n138: \n139: # Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets\n140: /create:skill-parent my-loop-workflows create --modes research,review,ai-council :confirm\n141: \n142: # Create a rooted feature catalog package\n143: /create:feature-catalog system-spec-kit create :confirm\n144: \n145: # Update an existing testing playbook package\n146: /create:manual-testing-playbook system-spec-kit update :auto\n147: \n148: # Add a reference doc to an existing skill\n149: /create:skill my-skill reference-only debugging :confirm\n150: \n151: # Create a changelog from a completed spec folder\n152: /create:changelog specs/my-track/042-memory-upgrade :auto\n153: \n154: # Create a changelog for a specific component\n155: /create:changelog sk-doc --bump minor :confirm\n156: \n157: # Review what changed in a locally edited document\n158: /create:diff proposal.md --report proposal-diff.html :auto\n159: \n160: # Add a repo rule and wire it into REPO RULES.md\n161: /create:repo-rule \"how migrations get reviewed\" create :confirm\n162: \n163: # Author a spec packet's goal.md and print its chat slice\n164: /create:goal specs/my-track/001-feature top-level :confirm\n165: \n166: # Score a document against the Human Voice Rules without editing it\n167: /create:with-human-voice docs/overview.md score :auto\n168: ```\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 8. FAQ\n173: \n174: **Q: When should I use `create` vs `update` for feature-catalog and testing-playbook commands?**\n175: \n176: A: Use `create` when the package folder does not yet exist under the skill root. Use `update` when the package already exists and you want to add or revise content within it. Running `create` on an existing package will produce a conflict error.\n177: \n178: **Q: What does the `--chained` flag do on `/create:skill`?**\n179: \n180: A: The `--chained` flag signals that the command was dispatched from a parent workflow (for example, a `full-create` that hands off to a doc-only phase). It changes how the command reports completion and does not affect the output files. Remove it when running the command standalone.\n181: \n182: **Q: How does `/create:changelog` determine which version to assign?**\n183: \n184: A: The command reads the newest version in the target folder, including its generation folders such as `v3+/`, and picks the bump from the change. A breaking change, rewrite or migration is major. A new feature is minor. A hotfix or typo is build, and anything else is patch. Supply `--bump major`, `--bump minor`, `--bump patch` or `--bump build` to choose it yourself. If a file already exists at the new version, the BUILD segment increments until the name is free. In `:confirm` mode you can also select the version manually during execution.\n185: \n186: ---\n187: \n188: ## 9. TROUBLESHOOTING\n189: \n190: | Problem | Cause | Fix |\n191: |---------|-------|-----|\n192: | Phase 0 fails | @markdown agent not available | Verify agent files exist in the runtime path (`.skilled/agents/` or `.claude/agents/`) |\n193: | YAML workflow not found | Missing asset file | Check `assets/` contains the matching YAML for operation and mode |\n194: | Skill not found for skill operation | Wrong skill name | Use the exact folder name from `.skilled/skills/` |\n195: | Catalog or playbook update target missing | `update` used before the package exists | Re-run with `create` or point to the correct skill root |\n196: | Playbook scaffolds forbidden sidecar files | Using an outdated package shape | Use `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, which keeps review/orchestration guidance in `manual-testing-playbook.md` |\n197: | `--chained` has no effect | Only meaningful for chained skill doc-only operations | Remove flag when running standalone |\n198: | `changelog` wrong component | File path mapping mismatch | Pass the component as the first argument, such as `sk-git` or `sk-create-changelog`, or select it in `:confirm` mode |\n199: | `changelog` version conflict | File already exists | Command auto-increments BUILD segment. Specify `--bump` to override |\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: ## 10. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n204: \n205: | Document | Purpose |\n206: |----------|---------|\n207: | [Parent: OpenCode Commands](../README.txt) | Overview of all command groups |\n208: | [sk-doc SKILL.md](../../skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md) | Templates and standards used by create commands |\n209: | [references/README.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md) | Standards for rooted feature catalog packages |\n210: | [references/README.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md) | Standards for rooted testing playbook packages |\n211: | [agent-template.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md) | Agent creation template |\n212: | [command-template.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md) | Command creation template |\n213: | [references/README.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/README.md) | Skill creation workflow route-map (includes \"Parent Skills with Nested Mode Packets\") |\n214: | [parent-skill-hub-template.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md) | Parent-skill hub `SKILL.md` template |\n215: | [parent-skill-registry-template.json](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json) | Parent-skill `mode-registry.json` template |","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/README.txt, lines 1-215\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Create Commands\"\n3: description: \"Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, docs, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"create command\"\n6:   - \"scaffold component\"\n7:   - \"create agent\"\n8:   - \"create skill\"\n9:   - \"create readme\"\n10:   - \"create feature catalog\"\n11:   - \"create testing playbook\"\n12:   - \"create changelog\"\n13:   - \"create chart\"\n14:   - \"create diagram\"\n15:   - \"create diff\"\n16:   - \"create repo rule\"\n17:   - \"apply human voice\"\n18: ---\n19: \n20: # Create Commands\n21: \n22: > Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, charts, diagrams, diff reports and repo rules with proper templates and validation.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n27: \n28: The `create` command group scaffolds OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, and standalone visual and prose artifacts. All commands follow a structured YAML workflow and support `:auto` (no approval prompts) and `:confirm` (pause at each step) execution modes.\n29: \n30: The table in section 3 lists every command in this folder. When a command file is added here, add its row there too; a missing row is the failure mode this index has hit before.\n31: \n32: All shipped `create` commands run Phase 0 (@markdown agent self-verification).\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 2. PURPOSE\n37: \n38: Use this index to understand which `/create:*` command owns a given scaffolding workflow, which argument shape it expects, and which package contract or artifact family it generates.\n39: \n40: This document is a routing and reference surface only. Run the command entrypoint itself for execution, setup prompting, and YAML workflow dispatch.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. COMMANDS\n45: | Command | Invocation | Description |\n46: |---------|------------|-------------|\n47: | **agent** | `/create:agent <agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, and behavioral rules |\n48: | **benchmark** | `/create:benchmark <skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> [create\\|update] --family=<family> [--benchmark-id <id>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages |\n49: | **changelog** | `/create:changelog <spec-folder-or-component> [--bump <major\\|minor\\|patch\\|build\\|auto>] [--release] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a global changelog entry under `.skilled/changelog/` that search can find, with a GitHub release for the `skilled` line when asked |\n50: | **command** | `/create:command <command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or update an OpenCode slash command set with router and `:auto`/`:confirm` workflow assets |\n51: | **diff** | `/create:diff <target-document \\| --before old --after new> [--report out.html] [--view unified\\|side-by-side] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a self-contained before/after document diff report via the create-diff engine |\n52: | **feature-catalog** | `/create:feature-catalog <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or update a rooted `feature-catalog/` package using the shipped `sk-doc` contract |\n53: | **goal** | `/create:goal <packet path> [top-level\\|phase-parent\\|child\\|retrofit\\|phase-add\\|amend] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Author or revise a packet `goal.md` for top-level, phase-parent, child, retrofit, phase-add and amend |\n54: | **manual-testing-playbook** | `/create:manual-testing-playbook <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or update a rooted `manual-testing-playbook/` package using the shipped `sk-doc` contract |\n55: | **readme** | `/create:readme <target> [--type <project\\|component\\|feature\\|skill>] [--output <path>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Folder README creation with `sk-doc` quality standards |\n56: | **repo-rule** | `/create:repo-rule <what the rule should bind> [create\\|revise\\|retire] [--rule <name>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create, revise or retire a repo rule under `repo-rules/`, wired into `REPO RULES.md` |\n57: | **skill** | `/create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Unified skill workflow (full-create, full-update, reference-only, asset-only) |\n58: | **skill-parent** | `/create:skill-parent <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--modes <m1,m2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, `mode-registry.json` source of truth, and a root `ROUTER.md` stage-two control document) |\n59: | **with-human-voice** | `/create:with-human-voice <file or passage> [apply\\|score] [--include-code] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules with a scope gate and a re-scan |\n60: \n61: ### README Types\n62: \n63: The `readme` operation in `/create:readme` accepts a `--type` flag:\n64: \n65: | Type | Use Case |\n66: |------|----------|\n67: | `project` | Root-level project documentation |\n68: | `component` | Reusable module or library |\n69: | `feature` | Specific feature or system |\n70: | `skill` | AI skill supplementary documentation |\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 4. STRUCTURE\n75: \n76: ```\n77: create/\n78: ├── agent.md                      # /create:agent command\n79: ├── benchmark.md                  # /create:benchmark command\n80: ├── changelog.md                  # /create:changelog command\n81: ├── command.md                    # /create:command command\n82: ├── diff.md                       # /create:diff command\n83: ├── feature-catalog.md            # /create:feature-catalog command\n84: ├── goal.md                       # /create:goal command\n85: ├── manual-testing-playbook.md    # /create:manual-testing-playbook command\n86: ├── readme.md                     # /create:readme — folder README command\n87: ├── repo-rule.md                  # /create:repo-rule command\n88: ├── skill.md                      # /create:skill command\n89: ├── skill-parent.md               # /create:skill-parent command\n90: ├── with-human-voice.md           # /create:with-human-voice command\n91: └── assets/                       # One auto YAML, one confirm YAML and one presentation\n92:                                   # contract per command; see the folder itself for the\n93:                                   # live file set rather than a count kept here\n94: ```\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: ## 5. INSTRUCTIONS\n99: \n100: 1. Pick the command family that matches the artifact you need.\n101: 2. Use the canonical command entrypoint, not a deprecated alias.\n102: 3. Supply `:auto` for autonomous execution or `:confirm` for checkpointed execution.\n103: 4. For rooted documentation packages, use the package-specific commands instead of composing the files manually.\n104: 5. If the command performs file modifications, keep it attached to the active spec workflow.\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 6. EXECUTION MODES\n109: \n110: | Mode | Suffix | Behavior |\n111: |------|--------|----------|\n112: | **Auto** | `:auto` | Execute all steps without approval prompts |\n113: | **Confirm** | `:confirm` | Pause at each step and wait for user approval |\n114: \n115: Each mode loads a separate YAML workflow from `assets/` when that command ships YAML assets:\n116: - Auto: `create-<command>-auto.yaml`\n117: - Confirm: `create-<command>-confirm.yaml`\n118: \n119: The `--chained` flag on `/create:skill` doc-only operations indicates parent workflow handoff.\n120: \n121: The documentation-package commands preserve the live `sk-doc` contracts:\n122: - `/create:feature-catalog` produces `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` plus bare descriptive-slug category folders (the root catalog owns display order)\n123: - `/create:manual-testing-playbook` produces `manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` plus bare descriptive-slug category folders (the root playbook owns display order) and no sidecar review/ledger files\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: ## 7. USAGE EXAMPLES\n128: \n129: ```bash\n130: # Create a new agent in auto mode\n131: /create:agent my-analyzer \"Code analysis specialist\" :auto\n132: \n133: # Create a README for a specific folder\n134: /create:readme readme .skilled/skills/my-skill --type skill :confirm\n135: \n136: # Create a full skill\n137: /create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n138: \n139: # Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets\n140: /create:skill-parent my-loop-workflows create --modes research,review,ai-council :confirm\n141: \n142: # Create a rooted feature catalog package\n143: /create:feature-catalog system-spec-kit create :confirm\n144: \n145: # Update an existing testing playbook package\n146: /create:manual-testing-playbook system-spec-kit update :auto\n147: \n148: # Add a reference doc to an existing skill\n149: /create:skill my-skill reference-only debugging :confirm\n150: \n151: # Create a changelog from a completed spec folder\n152: /create:changelog specs/my-track/042-memory-upgrade :auto\n153: \n154: # Create a changelog for a specific component\n155: /create:changelog sk-doc --bump minor :confirm\n156: \n157: # Review what changed in a locally edited document\n158: /create:diff proposal.md --report proposal-diff.html :auto\n159: \n160: # Add a repo rule and wire it into REPO RULES.md\n161: /create:repo-rule \"how migrations get reviewed\" create :confirm\n162: \n163: # Author a spec packet's goal.md and print its chat slice\n164: /create:goal specs/my-track/001-feature top-level :confirm\n165: \n166: # Score a document against the Human Voice Rules without editing it\n167: /create:with-human-voice docs/overview.md score :auto\n168: ```\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 8. FAQ\n173: \n174: **Q: When should I use `create` vs `update` for feature-catalog and testing-playbook commands?**\n175: \n176: A: Use `create` when the package folder does not yet exist under the skill root. Use `update` when the package already exists and you want to add or revise content within it. Running `create` on an existing package will produce a conflict error.\n177: \n178: **Q: What does the `--chained` flag do on `/create:skill`?**\n179: \n180: A: The `--chained` flag signals that the command was dispatched from a parent workflow (for example, a `full-create` that hands off to a doc-only phase). It changes how the command reports completion and does not affect the output files. Remove it when running the command standalone.\n181: \n182: **Q: How does `/create:changelog` determine which version to assign?**\n183: \n184: A: The command reads the newest version in the target folder, including its generation folders such as `v3+/`, and picks the bump from the change. A breaking change, rewrite or migration is major. A new feature is minor. A hotfix or typo is build, and anything else is patch. Supply `--bump major`, `--bump minor`, `--bump patch` or `--bump build` to choose it yourself. If a file already exists at the new version, the BUILD segment increments until the name is free. In `:confirm` mode you can also select the version manually during execution.\n185: \n186: ---\n187: \n188: ## 9. TROUBLESHOOTING\n189: \n190: | Problem | Cause | Fix |\n191: |---------|-------|-----|\n192: | Phase 0 fails | @markdown agent not available | Verify agent files exist in the runtime path (`.skilled/agents/` or `.claude/agents/`) |\n193: | YAML workflow not found | Missing asset file | Check `assets/` contains the matching YAML for operation and mode |\n194: | Skill not found for skill operation | Wrong skill name | Use the exact folder name from `.skilled/skills/` |\n195: | Catalog or playbook update target missing | `update` used before the package exists | Re-run with `create` or point to the correct skill root |\n196: | Playbook scaffolds forbidden sidecar files | Using an outdated package shape | Use `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, which keeps review/orchestration guidance in `manual-testing-playbook.md` |\n197: | `--chained` has no effect | Only meaningful for chained skill doc-only operations | Remove flag when running standalone |\n198: | `changelog` wrong component | File path mapping mismatch | Pass the component as the first argument, such as `sk-git` or `sk-create-changelog`, or select it in `:confirm` mode |\n199: | `changelog` version conflict | File already exists | Command auto-increments BUILD segment. Specify `--bump` to override |\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: ## 10. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n204: \n205: | Document | Purpose |\n206: |----------|---------|\n207: | [Parent: OpenCode Commands](../README.txt) | Overview of all command groups |\n208: | [sk-doc SKILL.md](../../skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md) | Templates and standards used by create commands |\n209: | [references/README.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-feature-catalog/references/README.md) | Standards for rooted feature catalog packages |\n210: | [references/README.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/references/README.md) | Standards for rooted testing playbook packages |\n211: | [agent-template.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-agent/assets/agent-template.md) | Agent creation template |\n212: | [command-template.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-command/assets/command-template.md) | Command creation template |\n213: | [references/README.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/README.md) | Skill creation workflow route-map (includes \"Parent Skills with Nested Mode Packets\") |\n214: | [parent-skill-hub-template.md](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-hub-template.md) | Parent-skill hub `SKILL.md` template |\n215: | [parent-skill-registry-template.json](../../skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/parent-skill/parent-skill-registry-template.json) | Parent-skill `mode-registry.json` template |"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/README.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582790354,"end":1794582791139}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582791146,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5784280001AErYJecw5ZVQnT","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5780ce7001Frrw7haNt4XeUX","type":"tool","id":"call_46225f72c4b24265a52b516c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/README.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/README.txt, lines 1-297\n1: ---\n2: title: \"OpenCode Commands\"\n3: description: \"OpenCode slash commands: component creation, deep loops, prompts, continuity and spec kit workflows.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"opencode commands\"\n6:   - \"slash commands\"\n7:   - \"command reference\"\n8:   - \"available commands\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # OpenCode Commands\n12: \n13: > Slash commands that provide structured workflows for component creation, deep loops, prompt improvement, packet continuity, and spec kit operations.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: Commands are invoked as slash commands (e.g., `/create:feature-catalog`, `/deep:review`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:plan`). Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\n20: \n21: Commands are organized into six groups:\n22: \n23: | Group | Path | Commands | Purpose |\n24: |-------|------|----------|---------|\n25: | **create** | `commands/create/` | 13 | Scaffold OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules |\n26: | **deep** | `commands/deep/` | 3 | Deep research, review and AI council loops |\n27: | **doctor** | `commands/doctor/` | 17 | Setup overview, problem-to-command routing, spec-kit retrieval, skill advisor, deep-loop, runtime-mirror, sk-code setup, CI workflow switches, skill format check, git hook and standards, MCP, release-update, project-repo symlink check, link and unlink, ordered install guide, vendored-tree overlay status, apply and re-pin, root instruction-file check and embed, and environment-switch diagnostics |\n28: | **design** | `commands/design/` | 3 | Style Reference extraction, standalone charts and diagrams |\n29: | **prompt** | `commands/prompt/` | 1 | Prompt engineering surface (`/prompt:improve`) via sk-prompt |\n30: | **speckit** | `commands/speckit/` | 7 | Spec folder workflows (plan, implement, resume and complete), context save (save), lexical search (search) and the manual trigger for the session relaunch loop (handoff) |\n31: \n32: One OpenCode-only command lives outside this tree: `/goal-opencode` manages the passive session goal via the `opencode-goal` plugin, so it is authored in `.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md`, beside that directory's links to these groups. The prompt-improvement surface lives in the `prompt` group as `prompt/improve.md` (invoked `/prompt:improve`).\n33: \n34: Each group's command count above is the number of command files in that folder. When a command is added, update the count and its row in section 4. A group whose file set outgrew this index is the failure mode this document has hit before.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 2. PURPOSE\n39: \n40: Use this document as the top-level routing reference for the OpenCode slash-command surface. It explains which command group owns which workflow and points readers to the canonical sub-index for deeper command-family detail.\n41: \n42: This file is descriptive only. The executable contract for any workflow lives in the command entrypoint markdown file itself.\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## 3. STRUCTURE\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: command/\n50: ├── prompt/                   # Prompt engineering command group\n51: │   └── improve.md            # Canonical prompt improvement command (/prompt:improve)\n52: ├── create/                   # Component creation commands, see create/README.txt for the\n53: │   │                         # full thirteen-command table and per-command invocations\n54: │   ├── agent.md              # Create new agent\n55: │   ├── benchmark.md          # Promote a curated MCP benchmark folder\n56: │   ├── changelog.md          # Create changelog entry\n57: │   ├── command.md            # Create or update OpenCode slash command set\n58: │   ├── diff.md               # Create a before/after document diff report\n59: │   ├── feature-catalog.md    # Create or update feature catalog package\n60: │   ├── goal.md               # Author or revise a packet goal.md\n61: │   ├── manual-testing-playbook.md   # Create or update manual testing playbook package\n62: │   ├── readme.md             # Create a folder README\n63: │   ├── repo-rule.md          # Create, revise or retire a repo rule\n64: │   ├── skill.md              # Create or update skill package/files\n65: │   ├── skill-parent.md       # Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets\n66: │   ├── with-human-voice.md   # Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules\n67: │   └── assets/               # YAML workflow and presentation contracts\n68: ├── deep/                     # Deep-loop commands\n69: │   ├── ai-council.md         # Multi-seat AI council planning\n70: │   ├── research.md           # Iterative deep research workflow\n71: │   ├── review.md             # Iterative code review workflow\n72: │   └── assets/               # YAML workflow definitions\n73: ├── doctor/                   # Diagnostic commands, one per owner\n74: │   ├── speckit.md            # Spec-kit retrieval diagnostics\n75: │   ├── skill-advisor.md      # Skill advisor tune, rebuild and audits\n76: │   ├── deep-loop.md          # Deep-loop graph and convergence diagnostics\n77: │   ├── runtime-mirrors.md    # Runtime mirror parity check\n78: │   ├── sk-code.md            # sk-code setup battery with a repair per failing leg\n79: │   ├── ci.md                 # GitHub Actions workflow report, scaffold and switch toggle\n80: │   ├── git.md                # Git hook gate settings and sk-git standards\n81: │   ├── mcp.md                # Diagnose/install MCP infrastructure\n82: │   ├── update.md             # Release-aware framework updater\n83: │   ├── env.md                # Environment switch inspection\n84: │   ├── setup.md              # Doctor targets plus the read-only setup checks\n85: │   ├── assets/               # YAML workflow definitions\n86: │   └── scripts/              # Diagnostic scripts\n87: ├── design/                    # Design extraction commands\n88: │   ├── extract.md             # Extract a measured Style Reference DESIGN.md\n89: │   ├── chart.md              # Author a standalone HTML data chart\n90: │   ├── diagram.md            # Create an HTML/SVG diagram or a validated ASCII flowchart\n91: │   └── assets/                # Auto/confirm/presentation workflow assets\n92: └── speckit/                  # Spec folder workflow, continuity write and retrieval commands\n93:     ├── complete.md           # Full end-to-end workflow\n94:     ├── handoff.md            # Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop\n95:     ├── implement.md          # Execute pre-planned work\n96:     ├── plan.md               # Spec through plan only\n97:     ├── resume.md             # Resume existing spec work\n98:     ├── save.md               # Save conversation context into packet continuity\n99:     ├── search.md             # Lexical retrieval: trigger-index lookup plus ripgrep recipes\n100:     └── assets/               # YAML workflow definitions, plus save/search presentation contracts\n101: ```\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 4. COMMAND GROUPS\n106: \n107: ### Create Commands\n108: \n109: Scaffold OpenCode components using the `sk-doc` skill. Each command supports `:auto` and `:confirm` execution modes with corresponding YAML workflow files in `create/assets/`.\n110: \n111: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n112: |---------|------------|---------|\n113: | Agent | `/create:agent <agent_name>` | Create agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules |\n114: | Benchmark | `/create:benchmark <skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> --family=<family>` | Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages |\n115: | Changelog | `/create:changelog <spec-folder-or-component>` | Create a global changelog entry in `.skilled/changelog/` from recent work |\n116: | Command | `/create:command <command_invocation> [command_request]` | Create or update an OpenCode slash command set |\n117: | Diff | `/create:diff <document> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a self-contained before/after document diff report |\n118: | Feature Catalog | `/create:feature-catalog <skill> [create\\|update]` | Create or update a rooted `feature-catalog/` package |\n119: | Folder README | `/create:readme <target>` | Folder README workflow |\n120: | Goal (Packet) | `/create:goal <packet path> [top-level\\|phase-parent\\|child\\|retrofit\\|phase-add\\|amend]` | Author or revise a spec packet's `goal.md` from its own sources |\n121: | Parent Skill | `/create:skill-parent <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--modes <m1,m2,...>]` | Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, registry source of truth) |\n122: | Repo Rule | `/create:repo-rule <what the rule should bind> [create\\|revise\\|retire]` | Create, revise or retire a repo rule under `repo-rules/`, wired into `REPO RULES.md` |\n123: | Skill | `/create:skill <name> <operation> [type]` | Unified skill create/update/reference/asset workflow |\n124: | Testing Playbook | `/create:manual-testing-playbook <skill> [create\\|update]` | Create or update a rooted `manual-testing-playbook/` package |\n125: | With Human Voice | `/create:with-human-voice <file or passage> [apply\\|score]` | Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules |\n126: \n127: ### Doctor Commands\n128: \n129: Seventeen command files cover the diagnostic surface, one per owner, with one entry point that names the others. Backed by `_routes.yaml`, `mcp-doctor.sh`, interactive YAML workflows, and the live environment switch reference.\n130: \n131: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n132: |---------|------------|---------|\n133: | Setup | `/doctor:setup` | List every doctor target with what it checks, run the read-only setup checks once and name the repair command for each failing leg |\n134: | Helper | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem from its route phrases, show the class and the reason on every line, run a read-only pick in place and hand a writing pick back as one line |\n135: | Spec-Kit Retrieval | `/doctor:speckit` | Diagnose the generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep retrieval recipes |\n136: | Skill Advisor | `/doctor:skill-advisor <target> [flags]` | Re-tune routing, rebuild the skill graph, or audit graph freshness, router reach, description budget and parent-skill structure |\n137: | Deep-Loop | `/doctor:deep-loop [--scope=<scope>]` | Diagnose deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n138: | Runtime Mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Check that the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors are in sync with `.skilled` |\n139: | sk-code Setup | `/doctor:sk-code [setup\\|quality] [--prompt=<text>] [--dry-run]` | Run the sk-code setup battery read-only, or check the repository quality config and create `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once after an approved plan, naming each repair |\n140: | CI | `/doctor:ci [report\\|scaffold\\|toggle] [--json] [--sha=<sha>] [--no-gh]` | List GitHub Actions workflows with their switch state, scaffold a new workflow or toggle one CI switch |\n141: | Git | `/doctor:git <hooks\\|standards\\|setup> [--dry-run]` | Switch shipped git hook gates on or off in git config, change the commit, PR and branch rules in `.sk-git/` and check which sk-git settings are live |\n142: | MCP Debug | `/doctor:mcp debug [--fix]` | Diagnose Code Mode build, UTCP configuration, credentials, and runtime registration |\n143: | MCP Install | `/doctor:mcp install [--runtime <name>]` | Install Code Mode and configure its UTCP file and selected runtime |\n144: | Update | `/doctor:update [check\\|align\\|apply\\|rollback\\|record-base\\|compat]` | Release-aware spec-kit updater with read-only check, decision alignment, gated apply, rollback, base-recording and compat workflows, where compat moves a v3 spec layout to v4 behind two approvals |\n145: | Environment Switches | `/doctor:env [list \\| <section> \\| <VARIABLE>] [--dry-run]` | Inspect documented environment switches and optionally save a confirmed preference |\n146: | Skill Format Check | `/doctor:sk-skill [check\\|convert] [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>] [--dry-run]` | Report how far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format row by row, or how far a skill or mode is from a hub's eleven surfaces, and convert one skill after a plan and a yes |\n147: | Agents Instruction File | `/doctor:agents-md [check\\|embed\\|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run] [--plan-digest <digest>]` | Report what the root `AGENTS.md` holds against the shipped template row by row, embed the template plus the repository block after a plan and its digest, and restore one recorded run |\n148: | Symlink | `/doctor:symlink [check\\|link\\|unlink] [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--mode <shape>] [--ignore <where>] [--plan-digest <digest>] [--run <dir>] [--yes] [--dry-run]` | Report, create or remove the links that put `.skilled` and the chosen runtime folders into another project repo, as a whole-folder link or a real folder holding one link per entry, and write only against the plan digest the operator approved |\n149: | Install Guide | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Check the two builds, ask for the target repo, runtimes, link shape and instruction choice in one prompt, run the symlink check and print the ordered setup commands, naming each writing command without ever running one |\n150: | Overlay | `/doctor:overlay [status\\|apply\\|repin] [--json] [--audit] [--root <dir>] [--capture\\|--adopt <path>\\|--relayout] [--upstream\\|--to\\|--rollback <value>]` | Report which overlay destinations in a vendored Skilled tree are out of sync and why, then put the overlays back, capture one live edit into its overlay source, adopt one unowned vendored path as a new overlay, move each overlay source kept off its layout path onto it, or re-pin the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan with a rollback, after one yes |\n151: \n152: ### Deep Commands\n153: \n154: Run long-form, stateful deep-loop workflows. Each command supports `:auto` and `:confirm` execution modes with corresponding YAML workflow files in `deep/assets/`.\n155: \n156: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n157: |---------|------------|---------|\n158: | AI Council | `/deep:ai-council <question> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Multi-seat planning and convergence checks |\n159: | Research Loop | `/deep:research <topic> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Iterative technical investigation with convergence |\n160: | Review Loop | `/deep:review <target> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Iterative code review with severity-weighted findings |\n161: \n162: ### Design Commands\n163: \n164: Extract a measured Style Reference from a live site using the `sk-design-md-generator` skill.\n165: \n166: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n167: |---------|------------|---------|\n168: | Extract | `/design:extract <live-url> --output <dir> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Extract a measured Style Reference DESIGN.md |\n169: | Chart | `/design:chart <target-chart.html> <what the reader compares>` | Author a standalone HTML chart from a catalog of 21 forms |\n170: | Diagram | `/design:diagram <target.html\\|target.md> [description\\|--import <src>]` | Create an HTML/SVG diagram, an ASCII/markdown flowchart, or a draw.io/Mermaid redraw |\n171: \n172: ### Root Commands\n173: \n174: Root commands have no group prefix.\n175: \n176: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n177: |---------|------------|---------|\n178: | Prompt | `/prompt:improve <prompt_or_topic> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or improve prompts using frameworks, DEPTH thinking, and CLEAR scoring |\n179: | Goal (OpenCode) | `/goal-opencode <condition>` | Set/show/pause/clear/complete a durable session-completion goal via the `opencode-goal` plugin. Authored in `.opencode/commands/`, not in this tree |\n180: \n181: ### Spec Kit Commands\n182: \n183: Structured workflows for the spec folder development lifecycle, plus packet continuity write and lexical retrieval.\n184: \n185: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n186: |---------|------------|---------|\n187: | Complete | `/speckit:complete <description>` | Full end-to-end workflow (14+ steps) |\n188: | Handoff | `/speckit:handoff (no arguments)` | Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop |\n189: | Implement | `/speckit:implement <spec-folder>` | Execute pre-planned work (requires plan.md) |\n190: | Plan | `/speckit:plan <description> [--intake-only] [:with-phases]` | Planning workflow (spec through plan only). `--intake-only` publishes just `spec.md`, `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json`. `:with-phases` adds phase decomposition |\n191: | Resume | `/speckit:resume [spec-folder]` | Resume work on existing spec folder |\n192: | Save | `/speckit:save <spec-folder>` | Write conversation context into canonical spec-doc continuity surfaces |\n193: | Search | `/speckit:search <query> [--packet <spec-folder>] [--triggers\\|--paths\\|--count]` | Lexical retrieval: trigger-index lookup plus ripgrep recipes over spec docs and skill docs |\n194: \n195: ---\n196: \n197: ## 5. INSTRUCTIONS\n198: \n199: 1. Choose the command group that matches your intent: `create`, `deep`, `design`, `doctor`, `prompt` or `speckit`.\n200: 2. Use the canonical slash-command form `/<group>:<command>` unless the command is a root utility such as `/goal-opencode`.\n201: 3. Prefer the unified commands over historical split commands.\n202: 4. When a command supports `:auto` and `:confirm`, pick the mode that matches how much checkpointing you want.\n203: 5. Follow the family-specific index under `commands/<group>/README.txt` when one exists and you need detailed routing help.\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 6. USAGE\n208: \n209: ### Basic Invocation\n210: \n211: ```\n212: /create:feature-catalog system-spec-kit create :confirm\n213: /create:manual-testing-playbook system-spec-kit update :auto\n214: /create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n215: /prompt:improve $improve \"Build a clearer CLI handoff prompt\" :auto\n216: /speckit:save specs/<track>/007-feature\n217: /speckit:plan \"Add user authentication\" :auto\n218: ```\n219: \n220: ### With Execution Modes\n221: \n222: ```\n223: # Auto mode: execute without approval prompts\n224: /speckit:complete \"Add dark mode\" :auto\n225: \n226: # Confirm mode: pause at each step for approval\n227: /create:agent my-agent :confirm\n228: \n229: # With research phase\n230: /speckit:complete \"New feature\" :with-research\n231: \n232: # With automatic debug recovery notes\n233: ```\n234: \n235: ---\n236: \n237: ## 7. EXECUTION MODES\n238: \n239: Most commands in `create/`, `deep/`, `prompt`, and `speckit/` support two execution modes controlled by a suffix argument.\n240: \n241: | Mode | Suffix | Behavior |\n242: |------|--------|----------|\n243: | **Auto** | `:auto` | Execute all steps without approval prompts |\n244: | **Confirm** | `:confirm` | Pause at each step and wait for user approval |\n245: \n246: Each mode maps to a separate YAML workflow file in the command's `assets/` folder:\n247: - Auto: `<command>_auto.yaml`\n248: - Confirm: `<command>_confirm.yaml`\n249: \n250: The `speckit:complete` command supports two additional modes:\n251: - `:with-research` adds a research phase before planning\n252: \n253: ---\n254: \n255: ## 8. FAQ\n256: \n257: **Q: What is the difference between `:auto` and `:confirm` mode?**\n258: \n259: A: `:auto` runs all steps in sequence without pausing. `:confirm` stops at each step and waits for your approval before continuing. Use `:auto` when you trust the workflow and want speed. Use `:confirm` when you want to review or adjust each step before it executes.\n260: \n261: **Q: Can I use a command without specifying a mode?**\n262: \n263: A: Yes. Most commands fall back to `:confirm` behavior when no mode suffix is given. Check the command's frontmatter for its default if the behavior is unclear.\n264: \n265: **Q: When should I use `/speckit:plan` instead of `/speckit:complete`?**\n266: \n267: A: Use `/speckit:plan` when you want to produce a spec and plan document for review before any implementation begins. Use `/speckit:complete` when you are ready to run the full workflow end-to-end, including implementation.\n268: \n269: **Q: How do I recover a session that was interrupted?**\n270: \n271: A: Run `/speckit:resume`. This is the canonical recovery surface for packet work. It rebuilds context from `handover.md`, then `_memory.continuity`, then the packet's canonical spec docs. When you still need to find something afterwards, `/speckit:search` runs the lexical lanes over spec docs and skill docs.\n272: \n273: ---\n274: \n275: ## 9. TROUBLESHOOTING\n276: \n277: | Problem | Cause | Fix |\n278: |---------|-------|-----|\n279: | Command not recognized | Wrong invocation format | Use `/<group>:<command>` format (e.g., `/speckit:save`) |\n280: | Missing arguments error | Required argument not provided | Check the `argument-hint` in the command's frontmatter |\n281: | YAML workflow not found | Missing asset file | Verify `assets/` folder contains the corresponding YAML |\n282: | `create` vs `update` mismatch | Target package exists/does not exist as expected | Re-run the command with the matching operation |\n283: | Tool permission denied | Command lacks required tool | Check `allowed-tools` in command frontmatter |\n284: | Agent router has no request | Empty arguments passed | Provide an explicit request string |\n285: \n286: ---\n287: \n288: ## 10. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n289: \n290: | Document | Purpose |\n291: |----------|---------|\n292: | [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) | Framework defining gates, protocols, agent routing |\n293: | [Create Commands](create/README.txt) | Detailed index for all `/create:*` commands |\n294: | [Prompt Command](prompt/improve.md) | Canonical prompt improvement command |\n295: | [sk-doc SKILL.md](../skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md) | Documentation standards and component creation |\n296: | [system-spec-kit SKILL.md](../skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md) | Spec folder workflow and packet continuity |\n297: | [Spec Kit Commands](speckit/README.txt) | SpecKit plan, implement, complete, resume, save and search commands |","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/README.txt, lines 1-297\n1: ---\n2: title: \"OpenCode Commands\"\n3: description: \"OpenCode slash commands: component creation, deep loops, prompts, continuity and spec kit workflows.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"opencode commands\"\n6:   - \"slash commands\"\n7:   - \"command reference\"\n8:   - \"available commands\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # OpenCode Commands\n12: \n13: > Slash commands that provide structured workflows for component creation, deep loops, prompt improvement, packet continuity, and spec kit operations.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: Commands are invoked as slash commands (e.g., `/create:feature-catalog`, `/deep:review`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:plan`). Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\n20: \n21: Commands are organized into six groups:\n22: \n23: | Group | Path | Commands | Purpose |\n24: |-------|------|----------|---------|\n25: | **create** | `commands/create/` | 13 | Scaffold OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules |\n26: | **deep** | `commands/deep/` | 3 | Deep research, review and AI council loops |\n27: | **doctor** | `commands/doctor/` | 17 | Setup overview, problem-to-command routing, spec-kit retrieval, skill advisor, deep-loop, runtime-mirror, sk-code setup, CI workflow switches, skill format check, git hook and standards, MCP, release-update, project-repo symlink check, link and unlink, ordered install guide, vendored-tree overlay status, apply and re-pin, root instruction-file check and embed, and environment-switch diagnostics |\n28: | **design** | `commands/design/` | 3 | Style Reference extraction, standalone charts and diagrams |\n29: | **prompt** | `commands/prompt/` | 1 | Prompt engineering surface (`/prompt:improve`) via sk-prompt |\n30: | **speckit** | `commands/speckit/` | 7 | Spec folder workflows (plan, implement, resume and complete), context save (save), lexical search (search) and the manual trigger for the session relaunch loop (handoff) |\n31: \n32: One OpenCode-only command lives outside this tree: `/goal-opencode` manages the passive session goal via the `opencode-goal` plugin, so it is authored in `.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md`, beside that directory's links to these groups. The prompt-improvement surface lives in the `prompt` group as `prompt/improve.md` (invoked `/prompt:improve`).\n33: \n34: Each group's command count above is the number of command files in that folder. When a command is added, update the count and its row in section 4. A group whose file set outgrew this index is the failure mode this document has hit before.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 2. PURPOSE\n39: \n40: Use this document as the top-level routing reference for the OpenCode slash-command surface. It explains which command group owns which workflow and points readers to the canonical sub-index for deeper command-family detail.\n41: \n42: This file is descriptive only. The executable contract for any workflow lives in the command entrypoint markdown file itself.\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## 3. STRUCTURE\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: command/\n50: ├── prompt/                   # Prompt engineering command group\n51: │   └── improve.md            # Canonical prompt improvement command (/prompt:improve)\n52: ├── create/                   # Component creation commands, see create/README.txt for the\n53: │   │                         # full thirteen-command table and per-command invocations\n54: │   ├── agent.md              # Create new agent\n55: │   ├── benchmark.md          # Promote a curated MCP benchmark folder\n56: │   ├── changelog.md          # Create changelog entry\n57: │   ├── command.md            # Create or update OpenCode slash command set\n58: │   ├── diff.md               # Create a before/after document diff report\n59: │   ├── feature-catalog.md    # Create or update feature catalog package\n60: │   ├── goal.md               # Author or revise a packet goal.md\n61: │   ├── manual-testing-playbook.md   # Create or update manual testing playbook package\n62: │   ├── readme.md             # Create a folder README\n63: │   ├── repo-rule.md          # Create, revise or retire a repo rule\n64: │   ├── skill.md              # Create or update skill package/files\n65: │   ├── skill-parent.md       # Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets\n66: │   ├── with-human-voice.md   # Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules\n67: │   └── assets/               # YAML workflow and presentation contracts\n68: ├── deep/                     # Deep-loop commands\n69: │   ├── ai-council.md         # Multi-seat AI council planning\n70: │   ├── research.md           # Iterative deep research workflow\n71: │   ├── review.md             # Iterative code review workflow\n72: │   └── assets/               # YAML workflow definitions\n73: ├── doctor/                   # Diagnostic commands, one per owner\n74: │   ├── speckit.md            # Spec-kit retrieval diagnostics\n75: │   ├── skill-advisor.md      # Skill advisor tune, rebuild and audits\n76: │   ├── deep-loop.md          # Deep-loop graph and convergence diagnostics\n77: │   ├── runtime-mirrors.md    # Runtime mirror parity check\n78: │   ├── sk-code.md            # sk-code setup battery with a repair per failing leg\n79: │   ├── ci.md                 # GitHub Actions workflow report, scaffold and switch toggle\n80: │   ├── git.md                # Git hook gate settings and sk-git standards\n81: │   ├── mcp.md                # Diagnose/install MCP infrastructure\n82: │   ├── update.md             # Release-aware framework updater\n83: │   ├── env.md                # Environment switch inspection\n84: │   ├── setup.md              # Doctor targets plus the read-only setup checks\n85: │   ├── assets/               # YAML workflow definitions\n86: │   └── scripts/              # Diagnostic scripts\n87: ├── design/                    # Design extraction commands\n88: │   ├── extract.md             # Extract a measured Style Reference DESIGN.md\n89: │   ├── chart.md              # Author a standalone HTML data chart\n90: │   ├── diagram.md            # Create an HTML/SVG diagram or a validated ASCII flowchart\n91: │   └── assets/                # Auto/confirm/presentation workflow assets\n92: └── speckit/                  # Spec folder workflow, continuity write and retrieval commands\n93:     ├── complete.md           # Full end-to-end workflow\n94:     ├── handoff.md            # Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop\n95:     ├── implement.md          # Execute pre-planned work\n96:     ├── plan.md               # Spec through plan only\n97:     ├── resume.md             # Resume existing spec work\n98:     ├── save.md               # Save conversation context into packet continuity\n99:     ├── search.md             # Lexical retrieval: trigger-index lookup plus ripgrep recipes\n100:     └── assets/               # YAML workflow definitions, plus save/search presentation contracts\n101: ```\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 4. COMMAND GROUPS\n106: \n107: ### Create Commands\n108: \n109: Scaffold OpenCode components using the `sk-doc` skill. Each command supports `:auto` and `:confirm` execution modes with corresponding YAML workflow files in `create/assets/`.\n110: \n111: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n112: |---------|------------|---------|\n113: | Agent | `/create:agent <agent_name>` | Create agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules |\n114: | Benchmark | `/create:benchmark <skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> --family=<family>` | Author or update family-keyed benchmark packages |\n115: | Changelog | `/create:changelog <spec-folder-or-component>` | Create a global changelog entry in `.skilled/changelog/` from recent work |\n116: | Command | `/create:command <command_invocation> [command_request]` | Create or update an OpenCode slash command set |\n117: | Diff | `/create:diff <document> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create a self-contained before/after document diff report |\n118: | Feature Catalog | `/create:feature-catalog <skill> [create\\|update]` | Create or update a rooted `feature-catalog/` package |\n119: | Folder README | `/create:readme <target>` | Folder README workflow |\n120: | Goal (Packet) | `/create:goal <packet path> [top-level\\|phase-parent\\|child\\|retrofit\\|phase-add\\|amend]` | Author or revise a spec packet's `goal.md` from its own sources |\n121: | Parent Skill | `/create:skill-parent <skill-name> [create\\|update] [--modes <m1,m2,...>]` | Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, registry source of truth) |\n122: | Repo Rule | `/create:repo-rule <what the rule should bind> [create\\|revise\\|retire]` | Create, revise or retire a repo rule under `repo-rules/`, wired into `REPO RULES.md` |\n123: | Skill | `/create:skill <name> <operation> [type]` | Unified skill create/update/reference/asset workflow |\n124: | Testing Playbook | `/create:manual-testing-playbook <skill> [create\\|update]` | Create or update a rooted `manual-testing-playbook/` package |\n125: | With Human Voice | `/create:with-human-voice <file or passage> [apply\\|score]` | Apply or score prose against the Human Voice Rules |\n126: \n127: ### Doctor Commands\n128: \n129: Seventeen command files cover the diagnostic surface, one per owner, with one entry point that names the others. Backed by `_routes.yaml`, `mcp-doctor.sh`, interactive YAML workflows, and the live environment switch reference.\n130: \n131: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n132: |---------|------------|---------|\n133: | Setup | `/doctor:setup` | List every doctor target with what it checks, run the read-only setup checks once and name the repair command for each failing leg |\n134: | Helper | `/doctor:helper [<problem in plain words>] [--json]` | Rank the doctor commands that fit a described problem from its route phrases, show the class and the reason on every line, run a read-only pick in place and hand a writing pick back as one line |\n135: | Spec-Kit Retrieval | `/doctor:speckit` | Diagnose the generated trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep retrieval recipes |\n136: | Skill Advisor | `/doctor:skill-advisor <target> [flags]` | Re-tune routing, rebuild the skill graph, or audit graph freshness, router reach, description budget and parent-skill structure |\n137: | Deep-Loop | `/doctor:deep-loop [--scope=<scope>]` | Diagnose deep-loop coverage graphs and convergence for research, review and council runs |\n138: | Runtime Mirrors | `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Check that the agent, command, prompt and hook mirrors are in sync with `.skilled` |\n139: | sk-code Setup | `/doctor:sk-code [setup\\|quality] [--prompt=<text>] [--dry-run]` | Run the sk-code setup battery read-only, or check the repository quality config and create `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/repository/quality.json` once after an approved plan, naming each repair |\n140: | CI | `/doctor:ci [report\\|scaffold\\|toggle] [--json] [--sha=<sha>] [--no-gh]` | List GitHub Actions workflows with their switch state, scaffold a new workflow or toggle one CI switch |\n141: | Git | `/doctor:git <hooks\\|standards\\|setup> [--dry-run]` | Switch shipped git hook gates on or off in git config, change the commit, PR and branch rules in `.sk-git/` and check which sk-git settings are live |\n142: | MCP Debug | `/doctor:mcp debug [--fix]` | Diagnose Code Mode build, UTCP configuration, credentials, and runtime registration |\n143: | MCP Install | `/doctor:mcp install [--runtime <name>]` | Install Code Mode and configure its UTCP file and selected runtime |\n144: | Update | `/doctor:update [check\\|align\\|apply\\|rollback\\|record-base\\|compat]` | Release-aware spec-kit updater with read-only check, decision alignment, gated apply, rollback, base-recording and compat workflows, where compat moves a v3 spec layout to v4 behind two approvals |\n145: | Environment Switches | `/doctor:env [list \\| <section> \\| <VARIABLE>] [--dry-run]` | Inspect documented environment switches and optionally save a confirmed preference |\n146: | Skill Format Check | `/doctor:sk-skill [check\\|convert] [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>] [--dry-run]` | Report how far one skill, or the whole fleet, is from the Skilled format row by row, or how far a skill or mode is from a hub's eleven surfaces, and convert one skill after a plan and a yes |\n147: | Agents Instruction File | `/doctor:agents-md [check\\|embed\\|restore] [--json] [--root <dir>] [--dry-run] [--plan-digest <digest>]` | Report what the root `AGENTS.md` holds against the shipped template row by row, embed the template plus the repository block after a plan and its digest, and restore one recorded run |\n148: | Symlink | `/doctor:symlink [check\\|link\\|unlink] [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--mode <shape>] [--ignore <where>] [--plan-digest <digest>] [--run <dir>] [--yes] [--dry-run]` | Report, create or remove the links that put `.skilled` and the chosen runtime folders into another project repo, as a whole-folder link or a real folder holding one link per entry, and write only against the plan digest the operator approved |\n149: | Install Guide | `/doctor:install [--root <dir>] [--runtimes <list>] [--json]` | Check the two builds, ask for the target repo, runtimes, link shape and instruction choice in one prompt, run the symlink check and print the ordered setup commands, naming each writing command without ever running one |\n150: | Overlay | `/doctor:overlay [status\\|apply\\|repin] [--json] [--audit] [--root <dir>] [--capture\\|--adopt <path>\\|--relayout] [--upstream\\|--to\\|--rollback <value>]` | Report which overlay destinations in a vendored Skilled tree are out of sync and why, then put the overlays back, capture one live edit into its overlay source, adopt one unowned vendored path as a new overlay, move each overlay source kept off its layout path onto it, or re-pin the tree to a newer upstream commit over a staged plan with a rollback, after one yes |\n151: \n152: ### Deep Commands\n153: \n154: Run long-form, stateful deep-loop workflows. Each command supports `:auto` and `:confirm` execution modes with corresponding YAML workflow files in `deep/assets/`.\n155: \n156: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n157: |---------|------------|---------|\n158: | AI Council | `/deep:ai-council <question> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Multi-seat planning and convergence checks |\n159: | Research Loop | `/deep:research <topic> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Iterative technical investigation with convergence |\n160: | Review Loop | `/deep:review <target> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Iterative code review with severity-weighted findings |\n161: \n162: ### Design Commands\n163: \n164: Extract a measured Style Reference from a live site using the `sk-design-md-generator` skill.\n165: \n166: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n167: |---------|------------|---------|\n168: | Extract | `/design:extract <live-url> --output <dir> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Extract a measured Style Reference DESIGN.md |\n169: | Chart | `/design:chart <target-chart.html> <what the reader compares>` | Author a standalone HTML chart from a catalog of 21 forms |\n170: | Diagram | `/design:diagram <target.html\\|target.md> [description\\|--import <src>]` | Create an HTML/SVG diagram, an ASCII/markdown flowchart, or a draw.io/Mermaid redraw |\n171: \n172: ### Root Commands\n173: \n174: Root commands have no group prefix.\n175: \n176: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n177: |---------|------------|---------|\n178: | Prompt | `/prompt:improve <prompt_or_topic> [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Create or improve prompts using frameworks, DEPTH thinking, and CLEAR scoring |\n179: | Goal (OpenCode) | `/goal-opencode <condition>` | Set/show/pause/clear/complete a durable session-completion goal via the `opencode-goal` plugin. Authored in `.opencode/commands/`, not in this tree |\n180: \n181: ### Spec Kit Commands\n182: \n183: Structured workflows for the spec folder development lifecycle, plus packet continuity write and lexical retrieval.\n184: \n185: | Command | Invocation | Purpose |\n186: |---------|------------|---------|\n187: | Complete | `/speckit:complete <description>` | Full end-to-end workflow (14+ steps) |\n188: | Handoff | `/speckit:handoff (no arguments)` | Write the handoff note and prepare the session relaunch loop |\n189: | Implement | `/speckit:implement <spec-folder>` | Execute pre-planned work (requires plan.md) |\n190: | Plan | `/speckit:plan <description> [--intake-only] [:with-phases]` | Planning workflow (spec through plan only). `--intake-only` publishes just `spec.md`, `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json`. `:with-phases` adds phase decomposition |\n191: | Resume | `/speckit:resume [spec-folder]` | Resume work on existing spec folder |\n192: | Save | `/speckit:save <spec-folder>` | Write conversation context into canonical spec-doc continuity surfaces |\n193: | Search | `/speckit:search <query> [--packet <spec-folder>] [--triggers\\|--paths\\|--count]` | Lexical retrieval: trigger-index lookup plus ripgrep recipes over spec docs and skill docs |\n194: \n195: ---\n196: \n197: ## 5. INSTRUCTIONS\n198: \n199: 1. Choose the command group that matches your intent: `create`, `deep`, `design`, `doctor`, `prompt` or `speckit`.\n200: 2. Use the canonical slash-command form `/<group>:<command>` unless the command is a root utility such as `/goal-opencode`.\n201: 3. Prefer the unified commands over historical split commands.\n202: 4. When a command supports `:auto` and `:confirm`, pick the mode that matches how much checkpointing you want.\n203: 5. Follow the family-specific index under `commands/<group>/README.txt` when one exists and you need detailed routing help.\n204: \n205: ---\n206: \n207: ## 6. USAGE\n208: \n209: ### Basic Invocation\n210: \n211: ```\n212: /create:feature-catalog system-spec-kit create :confirm\n213: /create:manual-testing-playbook system-spec-kit update :auto\n214: /create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n215: /prompt:improve $improve \"Build a clearer CLI handoff prompt\" :auto\n216: /speckit:save specs/<track>/007-feature\n217: /speckit:plan \"Add user authentication\" :auto\n218: ```\n219: \n220: ### With Execution Modes\n221: \n222: ```\n223: # Auto mode: execute without approval prompts\n224: /speckit:complete \"Add dark mode\" :auto\n225: \n226: # Confirm mode: pause at each step for approval\n227: /create:agent my-agent :confirm\n228: \n229: # With research phase\n230: /speckit:complete \"New feature\" :with-research\n231: \n232: # With automatic debug recovery notes\n233: ```\n234: \n235: ---\n236: \n237: ## 7. EXECUTION MODES\n238: \n239: Most commands in `create/`, `deep/`, `prompt`, and `speckit/` support two execution modes controlled by a suffix argument.\n240: \n241: | Mode | Suffix | Behavior |\n242: |------|--------|----------|\n243: | **Auto** | `:auto` | Execute all steps without approval prompts |\n244: | **Confirm** | `:confirm` | Pause at each step and wait for user approval |\n245: \n246: Each mode maps to a separate YAML workflow file in the command's `assets/` folder:\n247: - Auto: `<command>_auto.yaml`\n248: - Confirm: `<command>_confirm.yaml`\n249: \n250: The `speckit:complete` command supports two additional modes:\n251: - `:with-research` adds a research phase before planning\n252: \n253: ---\n254: \n255: ## 8. FAQ\n256: \n257: **Q: What is the difference between `:auto` and `:confirm` mode?**\n258: \n259: A: `:auto` runs all steps in sequence without pausing. `:confirm` stops at each step and waits for your approval before continuing. Use `:auto` when you trust the workflow and want speed. Use `:confirm` when you want to review or adjust each step before it executes.\n260: \n261: **Q: Can I use a command without specifying a mode?**\n262: \n263: A: Yes. Most commands fall back to `:confirm` behavior when no mode suffix is given. Check the command's frontmatter for its default if the behavior is unclear.\n264: \n265: **Q: When should I use `/speckit:plan` instead of `/speckit:complete`?**\n266: \n267: A: Use `/speckit:plan` when you want to produce a spec and plan document for review before any implementation begins. Use `/speckit:complete` when you are ready to run the full workflow end-to-end, including implementation.\n268: \n269: **Q: How do I recover a session that was interrupted?**\n270: \n271: A: Run `/speckit:resume`. This is the canonical recovery surface for packet work. It rebuilds context from `handover.md`, then `_memory.continuity`, then the packet's canonical spec docs. When you still need to find something afterwards, `/speckit:search` runs the lexical lanes over spec docs and skill docs.\n272: \n273: ---\n274: \n275: ## 9. TROUBLESHOOTING\n276: \n277: | Problem | Cause | Fix |\n278: |---------|-------|-----|\n279: | Command not recognized | Wrong invocation format | Use `/<group>:<command>` format (e.g., `/speckit:save`) |\n280: | Missing arguments error | Required argument not provided | Check the `argument-hint` in the command's frontmatter |\n281: | YAML workflow not found | Missing asset file | Verify `assets/` folder contains the corresponding YAML |\n282: | `create` vs `update` mismatch | Target package exists/does not exist as expected | Re-run the command with the matching operation |\n283: | Tool permission denied | Command lacks required tool | Check `allowed-tools` in command frontmatter |\n284: | Agent router has no request | Empty arguments passed | Provide an explicit request string |\n285: \n286: ---\n287: \n288: ## 10. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n289: \n290: | Document | Purpose |\n291: |----------|---------|\n292: | [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) | Framework defining gates, protocols, agent routing |\n293: | [Create Commands](create/README.txt) | Detailed index for all `/create:*` commands |\n294: | [Prompt Command](prompt/improve.md) | Canonical prompt improvement command |\n295: | [sk-doc SKILL.md](../skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md) | Documentation standards and component creation |\n296: | [system-spec-kit SKILL.md](../skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md) | Spec folder workflow and packet continuity |\n297: | [Spec Kit Commands](speckit/README.txt) | SpecKit plan, implement, complete, resume, save and search commands |"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/README.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582790784,"end":1794582791146}}}}
