{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582795928,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5785613002p4L0SYJ98EohyX","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5784ad6001VU6QIIAo24UX2F","type":"tool","id":"call_00_1CR4tXJRxIyn04JjWMGZ0860","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md, lines 1-72\n1: ---\n2: description: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\n3: argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # /create:skill Router\n8: \n9: This command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n10: \n11: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n12: \n13: Route /create:skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n14: \n15: - Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n16: - Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Presentation contract | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` |\n25: | Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n26: | Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n33: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns user-visible wording and layout.\n34: \n35: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n36: 2. Run the presentation contract's Phase 0 verification and setup resolution.\n37: 3. Resolve operation from setup: `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only`.\n38: 4. Resolve execution mode from `$ARGUMENTS` or the setup answer: `:auto` or `:confirm`.\n39: 5. Load the workflow YAML bound to the resolved mode from the EXECUTION TARGETS table below.\n40: 6. Execute the selected YAML step by step and route to the resolved operation branch.\n41: 7. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, setup/status dashboards, and final result display.\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n46: \n47: | Mode | Target |\n48: |------|--------|\n49: | `:auto` | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n50: | `:confirm` or omitted mode | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n55: \n56: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`:\n57: \n58: - Startup questions, Phase 0 verification, setup dashboard, operation display, status display, completion template, and next-step text.\n59: \n60: The router must not invent visible wording for those surfaces; it only resolves operation, execution mode, and workflow selection.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n65: \n66: The bound workflow YAML (`create-skill-auto.yaml` for `:auto`, `create-skill-confirm.yaml` for `:confirm` or an omitted mode) runs the unified skill workflow step by step after Phase 0 verification and setup resolution, then routes to the resolved `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only` operation branch to create or update OpenCode skills.\n67: `:auto` executes autonomously.\n68: `:confirm` runs the same steps as an interactive checkpointed workflow.\n69: All user-facing prompts, setup/status dashboards, and result display come from the presentation contract, not this router.\n70: \n71: Generated routing follows the routing canon: `SMART ROUTING` is 8 to 12 lines of plain prose, every generated skill and mode packet owns a sibling `ROUTER.md` inside its own folder, and that file holds the machine router under a final `## MACHINE ROUTER` heading. The `SKILL.md` links to its sibling router in relative markdown and carries no `## MACHINE ROUTER` section itself. For a hub, that sibling file is the root `ROUTER.md`.\n72: ","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md, lines 1-72\n1: ---\n2: description: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\n3: argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # /create:skill Router\n8: \n9: This command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n10: \n11: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n12: \n13: Route /create:skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n14: \n15: - Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n16: - Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n21: \n22: | Purpose | Asset |\n23: |---------|-------|\n24: | Presentation contract | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` |\n25: | Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n26: | Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n31: \n32: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n33: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns user-visible wording and layout.\n34: \n35: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n36: 2. Run the presentation contract's Phase 0 verification and setup resolution.\n37: 3. Resolve operation from setup: `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only`.\n38: 4. Resolve execution mode from `$ARGUMENTS` or the setup answer: `:auto` or `:confirm`.\n39: 5. Load the workflow YAML bound to the resolved mode from the EXECUTION TARGETS table below.\n40: 6. Execute the selected YAML step by step and route to the resolved operation branch.\n41: 7. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, setup/status dashboards, and final result display.\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n46: \n47: | Mode | Target |\n48: |------|--------|\n49: | `:auto` | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n50: | `:confirm` or omitted mode | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n55: \n56: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`:\n57: \n58: - Startup questions, Phase 0 verification, setup dashboard, operation display, status display, completion template, and next-step text.\n59: \n60: The router must not invent visible wording for those surfaces; it only resolves operation, execution mode, and workflow selection.\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n65: \n66: The bound workflow YAML (`create-skill-auto.yaml` for `:auto`, `create-skill-confirm.yaml` for `:confirm` or an omitted mode) runs the unified skill workflow step by step after Phase 0 verification and setup resolution, then routes to the resolved `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only` operation branch to create or update OpenCode skills.\n67: `:auto` executes autonomously.\n68: `:confirm` runs the same steps as an interactive checkpointed workflow.\n69: All user-facing prompts, setup/status dashboards, and result display come from the presentation contract, not this router.\n70: \n71: Generated routing follows the routing canon: `SMART ROUTING` is 8 to 12 lines of plain prose, every generated skill and mode packet owns a sibling `ROUTER.md` inside its own folder, and that file holds the machine router under a final `## MACHINE ROUTER` heading. The `SKILL.md` links to its sibling router in relative markdown and carries no `## MACHINE ROUTER` section itself. For a hub, that sibling file is the root `ROUTER.md`.\n72: "}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582795795,"end":1794582795928}}}}
