{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794582803829,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"id":"prt_1d5787575001nx60DG4ubCou0I","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5786c71001J0GBWUWsbf9oho","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582804514,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d57877f8002jQsklo11IJ2RZY","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5786c71001J0GBWUWsbf9oho","type":"tool","id":"call_00_l1hUBAzMYvrLhOqqBfwi0742","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt, lines 1-169\n1: # /create:skill Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/create:skill`: startup questions, setup/status dashboards, operation display, and result templates. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Phase 0 Verification Display\n6: \n7: Run this automatic self-check before setup. This is not a user question.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: SELF-CHECK: Are you operating as @markdown OR under a valid chained parent handoff?\n11: \n12: Case A: Valid chained handoff detected with --chained\n13: - Required parent fields: skill_name, operation, execution_mode, parent_create_agent_verified=true\n14: - type is required only for reference-only or asset-only\n15: - If all fields are present: create_agent_verified = skipped-chained; chained_handoff_valid = true\n16: - If fields are missing: chained_handoff_valid = false and continue to Case B\n17: \n18: Case B: Standalone invocation\n19: - Verify @markdown indicators and sk-doc validation behavior\n20: - If present: create_agent_verified = true; phase_0_status = PASSED\n21: - If missing or uncertain: hard block\n22: ```\n23: \n24: Hard-block message:\n25: \n26: ```text\n27: This command requires @markdown for template-first generation and sk-doc validation.\n28: Restart with: @markdown /create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type]\n29: \n30: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"Markdown agent required\"\n31: ```\n32: \n33: ## 2. Auto Setup Resolution\n34: \n35: For `:auto`, resolve setup using the system auto-mode contract, then load `create-skill-auto.yaml` only when every required field is available.\n36: \n37: Pre-bound setup schema:\n38: \n39: ```yaml\n40: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n41:   skill_name: my-skill\n42:   operation: full-create\n43:   type: workflow\n44:   skill_path: .skilled/skills/\n45:   execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS\n46:   spec_choice: new\n47:   spec_path: <spec-folder>\n48:   memory_choice: skip\n49:   chained_handoff_valid: false\n50: ```\n51: \n52: Default resolution table:\n53: \n54: | Field | Required | Resolves Via | Default | Tier-2 Candidate |\n55: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n56: | `skill_name` | Yes | first positional token, marker, or chained parent value | none | No |\n57: | `operation` | Yes | second positional token, marker, or chained parent value | none | No |\n58: | `type` | Conditional | third positional token, marker, or chained value | none | Yes, when operation requires type |\n59: | `skill_path` | Yes | `--path`, marker, or default | `.skilled/skills/` | No |\n60: | `execution_mode` | Yes | `:auto`, `:confirm`, or marker | `AUTONOMOUS` under `:auto` | No |\n61: | `spec_choice` | Conditional | marker, chained value, or targeted choice | none | Yes, for full operations |\n62: | `spec_path` | Conditional | marker, derived from spec choice, or chained value | none | No |\n63: | `memory_choice` | No | marker, prior-work detection, or default | `skip` when no prior continuity exists | No |\n64: | `chained_handoff_valid` | No | `--chained` plus parent fields, marker, or default | `false` | No |\n65: \n66: ## 3. Consolidated Startup Prompt\n67: \n68: Ask only the applicable questions, together in one turn, through the question tool that `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §5 names for your runtime. Each question below becomes one tool question with its lettered options as the choices, and a free-text item such as a name or a path is answered through the tool's own free-text option. When the tool caps how many questions one call holds, make consecutive calls in the same turn. Only where §5 names no tool for this session, print the form below as text. Do not split these questions across turns.\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Before proceeding, please answer:\n72: \n73: Q0. Skill Name (if missing)\n74: Required format: hyphen-case.\n75: \n76: Q1. Operation (if missing)\n77: A) full-create - new skill end-to-end\n78: B) full-update - update existing skill and resources\n79: C) reference-only - create/update one reference document\n80: D) asset-only - create/update one asset document\n81: \n82: Q2. Type (only for reference-only or asset-only)\n83: For reference-only: workflow | patterns | debugging | tools | quick_ref\n84: For asset-only: template | lookup | example | guide\n85: \n86: Q3. Spec Folder (required for full-create/full-update)\n87: A) Existing\n88: B) New (new or unrelated work only)\n89: C) Related (Use a related folder, phase child, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track)\n90: D) Skip\n91: \n92: For reference-only/asset-only:\n93: A) Attach existing spec path for continuity tracking\n94: B) Skip spec linkage\n95: \n96: Q4. Prior Work Context (when the existing spec has prior continuity)\n97: A) Load handover plus implementation-summary continuity\n98: B) Load canonical spec docs up to a recent cap\n99: C) Skip\n100: \n101: Q5. Execution Mode (if no :auto/:confirm suffix)\n102: A) Interactive (:confirm)\n103: B) Autonomous (:auto)\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Hard stops:\n107: \n108: - Do not infer missing operation or type from context.\n109: - Do not split setup across multiple prompts.\n110: - Do not continue with missing required fields for the selected operation.\n111: \n112: ## 4. Setup Dashboard\n113: \n114: | Field | Required | Rule | Value |\n115: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n116: | `create_agent_verified` | Yes | `true` or `skipped-chained` | `[value]` |\n117: | `skill_name` | Yes | explicit, hyphen-case | `[value]` |\n118: | `operation` | Yes | one of four operation values | `[value]` |\n119: | `type` | Conditional | required for reference-only and asset-only | `[value]` |\n120: | `skill_path` | Yes | default if omitted | `[value]` |\n121: | `execution_mode` | Yes | `:auto` or `:confirm` | `[value]` |\n122: | `spec_choice` | Conditional | required for full-create and full-update | `[value]` |\n123: | `spec_path` | Conditional | required for A/B/C/D | `[value]` |\n124: | `memory_choice` | No | prior-work choice or skip | `[value]` |\n125: \n126: Proceed only when every required field validates.\n127: \n128: ## 5. Completion Result Template\n129: \n130: ```text\n131: Unified Skill Workflow Complete\n132: \n133: Skill: [skill_name]\n134: Operation: [operation]\n135: Type: [type or N/A]\n136: Mode: [:auto|:confirm]\n137: Target: [skill_root_or_target_file]\n138: \n139: Validation:\n140: - DQI: [score] ([band])\n141: - Hard minimum: 75\n142: - Operation target: [operation_target]\n143: [operation == full-create or full-update:]\n144: Human Voice:\n145:   - Per target: [path, hard blockers, mechanical deductions/ceiling, score/band or deduction density, scanner exit code]\n146:   - Judgment findings: [summary or None]\n147:   - Exemptions: [summary or None]\n148:   - Gate: [PASS only when all scans exit 0 and every absolute score is at least 85]\n149: \n150: Routing shape: SMART ROUTING is 8 to 12 lines of plain prose with a link to ./ROUTER.md. The machine router lives in that sibling ROUTER.md under a final ## MACHINE ROUTER heading, in every skill and every mode packet.\n151: \n152: [When operation is full-create or full-update:]\n153: Advisor/Index Handoff (operator-owned; this command did not mutate advisor state; standalone scope - H-only fields omitted):\n154: - graph-metadata.json: sole skill advisor identity; source for graph indexing\n155: - leaf-manifest.json: [fresh|stale|missing]\n156: - Refresh choice - run one when the advisor should include this change:\n157:   - Full advisor refresh: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json\n158:   - Graph-only refresh: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --skills-root \"$PWD/.skilled/skills\" --format json\n159: - Refresh status: NOT RUN (operator-owned; see .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md)\n160: \n161: [When operation is reference-only or asset-only:]\n162: Leaf-manifest freshness: [fresh|stale|missing] (narrow signal only - references/ and assets/ are always leaf roots; see advisor-index-handoff.md Branch Scope for why this branch does not render the full handoff)\n163: \n164: Context:\n165: - Spec path: [spec_path or none]\n166: - Memory saved: [yes/no]\n167: \n168: STATUS=[OK|CANCELLED|FAIL] PATH=[skill_root_or_target_file]\n169: ```","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt, lines 1-169\n1: # /create:skill Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/create:skill`: startup questions, setup/status dashboards, operation display, and result templates. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Phase 0 Verification Display\n6: \n7: Run this automatic self-check before setup. This is not a user question.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: SELF-CHECK: Are you operating as @markdown OR under a valid chained parent handoff?\n11: \n12: Case A: Valid chained handoff detected with --chained\n13: - Required parent fields: skill_name, operation, execution_mode, parent_create_agent_verified=true\n14: - type is required only for reference-only or asset-only\n15: - If all fields are present: create_agent_verified = skipped-chained; chained_handoff_valid = true\n16: - If fields are missing: chained_handoff_valid = false and continue to Case B\n17: \n18: Case B: Standalone invocation\n19: - Verify @markdown indicators and sk-doc validation behavior\n20: - If present: create_agent_verified = true; phase_0_status = PASSED\n21: - If missing or uncertain: hard block\n22: ```\n23: \n24: Hard-block message:\n25: \n26: ```text\n27: This command requires @markdown for template-first generation and sk-doc validation.\n28: Restart with: @markdown /create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type]\n29: \n30: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"Markdown agent required\"\n31: ```\n32: \n33: ## 2. Auto Setup Resolution\n34: \n35: For `:auto`, resolve setup using the system auto-mode contract, then load `create-skill-auto.yaml` only when every required field is available.\n36: \n37: Pre-bound setup schema:\n38: \n39: ```yaml\n40: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n41:   skill_name: my-skill\n42:   operation: full-create\n43:   type: workflow\n44:   skill_path: .skilled/skills/\n45:   execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS\n46:   spec_choice: new\n47:   spec_path: <spec-folder>\n48:   memory_choice: skip\n49:   chained_handoff_valid: false\n50: ```\n51: \n52: Default resolution table:\n53: \n54: | Field | Required | Resolves Via | Default | Tier-2 Candidate |\n55: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n56: | `skill_name` | Yes | first positional token, marker, or chained parent value | none | No |\n57: | `operation` | Yes | second positional token, marker, or chained parent value | none | No |\n58: | `type` | Conditional | third positional token, marker, or chained value | none | Yes, when operation requires type |\n59: | `skill_path` | Yes | `--path`, marker, or default | `.skilled/skills/` | No |\n60: | `execution_mode` | Yes | `:auto`, `:confirm`, or marker | `AUTONOMOUS` under `:auto` | No |\n61: | `spec_choice` | Conditional | marker, chained value, or targeted choice | none | Yes, for full operations |\n62: | `spec_path` | Conditional | marker, derived from spec choice, or chained value | none | No |\n63: | `memory_choice` | No | marker, prior-work detection, or default | `skip` when no prior continuity exists | No |\n64: | `chained_handoff_valid` | No | `--chained` plus parent fields, marker, or default | `false` | No |\n65: \n66: ## 3. Consolidated Startup Prompt\n67: \n68: Ask only the applicable questions, together in one turn, through the question tool that `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §5 names for your runtime. Each question below becomes one tool question with its lettered options as the choices, and a free-text item such as a name or a path is answered through the tool's own free-text option. When the tool caps how many questions one call holds, make consecutive calls in the same turn. Only where §5 names no tool for this session, print the form below as text. Do not split these questions across turns.\n69: \n70: ```text\n71: Before proceeding, please answer:\n72: \n73: Q0. Skill Name (if missing)\n74: Required format: hyphen-case.\n75: \n76: Q1. Operation (if missing)\n77: A) full-create - new skill end-to-end\n78: B) full-update - update existing skill and resources\n79: C) reference-only - create/update one reference document\n80: D) asset-only - create/update one asset document\n81: \n82: Q2. Type (only for reference-only or asset-only)\n83: For reference-only: workflow | patterns | debugging | tools | quick_ref\n84: For asset-only: template | lookup | example | guide\n85: \n86: Q3. Spec Folder (required for full-create/full-update)\n87: A) Existing\n88: B) New (new or unrelated work only)\n89: C) Related (Use a related folder, phase child, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track)\n90: D) Skip\n91: \n92: For reference-only/asset-only:\n93: A) Attach existing spec path for continuity tracking\n94: B) Skip spec linkage\n95: \n96: Q4. Prior Work Context (when the existing spec has prior continuity)\n97: A) Load handover plus implementation-summary continuity\n98: B) Load canonical spec docs up to a recent cap\n99: C) Skip\n100: \n101: Q5. Execution Mode (if no :auto/:confirm suffix)\n102: A) Interactive (:confirm)\n103: B) Autonomous (:auto)\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Hard stops:\n107: \n108: - Do not infer missing operation or type from context.\n109: - Do not split setup across multiple prompts.\n110: - Do not continue with missing required fields for the selected operation.\n111: \n112: ## 4. Setup Dashboard\n113: \n114: | Field | Required | Rule | Value |\n115: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n116: | `create_agent_verified` | Yes | `true` or `skipped-chained` | `[value]` |\n117: | `skill_name` | Yes | explicit, hyphen-case | `[value]` |\n118: | `operation` | Yes | one of four operation values | `[value]` |\n119: | `type` | Conditional | required for reference-only and asset-only | `[value]` |\n120: | `skill_path` | Yes | default if omitted | `[value]` |\n121: | `execution_mode` | Yes | `:auto` or `:confirm` | `[value]` |\n122: | `spec_choice` | Conditional | required for full-create and full-update | `[value]` |\n123: | `spec_path` | Conditional | required for A/B/C/D | `[value]` |\n124: | `memory_choice` | No | prior-work choice or skip | `[value]` |\n125: \n126: Proceed only when every required field validates.\n127: \n128: ## 5. Completion Result Template\n129: \n130: ```text\n131: Unified Skill Workflow Complete\n132: \n133: Skill: [skill_name]\n134: Operation: [operation]\n135: Type: [type or N/A]\n136: Mode: [:auto|:confirm]\n137: Target: [skill_root_or_target_file]\n138: \n139: Validation:\n140: - DQI: [score] ([band])\n141: - Hard minimum: 75\n142: - Operation target: [operation_target]\n143: [operation == full-create or full-update:]\n144: Human Voice:\n145:   - Per target: [path, hard blockers, mechanical deductions/ceiling, score/band or deduction density, scanner exit code]\n146:   - Judgment findings: [summary or None]\n147:   - Exemptions: [summary or None]\n148:   - Gate: [PASS only when all scans exit 0 and every absolute score is at least 85]\n149: \n150: Routing shape: SMART ROUTING is 8 to 12 lines of plain prose with a link to ./ROUTER.md. The machine router lives in that sibling ROUTER.md under a final ## MACHINE ROUTER heading, in every skill and every mode packet.\n151: \n152: [When operation is full-create or full-update:]\n153: Advisor/Index Handoff (operator-owned; this command did not mutate advisor state; standalone scope - H-only fields omitted):\n154: - graph-metadata.json: sole skill advisor identity; source for graph indexing\n155: - leaf-manifest.json: [fresh|stale|missing]\n156: - Refresh choice - run one when the advisor should include this change:\n157:   - Full advisor refresh: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json\n158:   - Graph-only refresh: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted --skills-root \"$PWD/.skilled/skills\" --format json\n159: - Refresh status: NOT RUN (operator-owned; see .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/shared/advisor-index-handoff.md)\n160: \n161: [When operation is reference-only or asset-only:]\n162: Leaf-manifest freshness: [fresh|stale|missing] (narrow signal only - references/ and assets/ are always leaf roots; see advisor-index-handoff.md Branch Scope for why this branch does not render the full handoff)\n163: \n164: Context:\n165: - Spec path: [spec_path or none]\n166: - Memory saved: [yes/no]\n167: \n168: STATUS=[OK|CANCELLED|FAIL] PATH=[skill_root_or_target_file]\n169: ```"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582804472,"end":1794582804514}}}}
