{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794582807268,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"id":"prt_1d57882e4001cP7Oqq4s7tIoPC","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5787c5c001akopz7L6rps5c6","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582807747,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d57882e8001Uu62axf5pskH0J","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5787c5c001akopz7L6rps5c6","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_UZB1wVhW4XXzS30d1o6g6658","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt, lines 1-157\n1: # Prompt Improve Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: Presentation source of truth for `/prompt:improve`. The router owns mode selection and asset loading. Workflow YAML owns execution. This file owns visible prompts, dashboard layout, and result displays.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: For `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt is the first visible response. Ask all applicable questions once, then wait. Never split them across multiple prompts.\n8: \n9: For `:auto`, do not show the consolidated prompt by default. Resolve setup through the auto-resolution table below and ask targeted questions only for fields that cannot be defaulted (Tier 2).\n10: \n11: ### Auto Pre-Bound Setup Answers\n12: \n13: Accept one optional marker block in the prompt body before applying defaults.\n14: \n15: ```yaml\n16: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n17:   prompt_input: Help users understand our API authentication flow\n18:   enhancement_mode: auto\n19:   save_choice: D\n20:   save_path: \"\"\n21:   execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS\n22:   dispatch_mode: INLINE\n23: ```\n24: \n25: Unknown fields warn. Malformed lines are parse errors. Marker values override flags; omitted fields fall back to defaults.\n26: \n27: ### Auto Resolution Table\n28: \n29: | Field | Required | Default | Tier 2 (targeted-ask when) |\n30: |-------|----------|---------|----------------------------|\n31: | `prompt_input` | Yes | none | Never inferred — fail fast if missing (see Auto Fail-Fast Display) |\n32: | `enhancement_mode` | Yes | `auto` (detect from content) | No |\n33: | `save_choice` | Yes | `D` (keep in conversation only) | Yes, when the user's request implies persisting a prompt library |\n34: | `save_path` | No | none unless `save_choice` is A/B/C | No |\n35: | `execution_mode` | Yes | `AUTONOMOUS` under `:auto` | No |\n36: | `dispatch_mode` | Yes | `AGENT` when `--agent` or resolved complexity `>= 7/10`, else `INLINE` | No |\n37: \n38: ### Consolidated Prompt Template\n39: \n40: Include only the questions whose fields are still unresolved after parsing `$ARGUMENTS`. Ask them together in one turn, through the question tool that `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §5 names for your runtime. Each question below becomes one tool question with its lettered options as the choices, and a free-text item such as a name or a path is answered through the tool's own free-text option. When the tool caps how many questions one call holds, make consecutive calls in the same turn. Only where §5 names no tool for this session, print the form below as text. Do not split these questions across turns.\n41: \n42: ```\n43: Before proceeding, please answer:\n44: \n45: Q0. Prompt Input (if not provided in command):\n46:     What prompt would you like to create or improve?\n47:     (paste prompt text, describe a topic, or specify a goal)\n48: \n49: Q1. Enhancement Mode (if no $mode prefix detected):\n50:     A) Auto-detect from content (Recommended)\n51:     B) $improve — Standard enhancement (all ten checklist rows)\n52:     C) $short — Quick refinement (four checklist rows)\n53:     D) $refine — Maximum optimization (all rows plus the quick test)\n54:     E) $raw — No checklist, format only\n55: \n56: Q2. Save Location (required):\n57:     A) Save to existing spec folder: [list if found]\n58:     B) Save to new spec folder\n59:     C) Save to specific path (inside the .opencode/specs/ tree)\n60:     D) Skip — keep in conversation only\n61: \n62: Q3. Execution Mode (if no :auto/:confirm suffix):\n63:     A) Autonomous — run end-to-end (Recommended)\n64:     B) Interactive — confirm after the checklist, the draft and the screen\n65: \n66: Q4. Dispatch Mode (if not auto-selected):\n67:     A) Inline skill — direct, in-context (default)\n68:     B) Agent — fresh @prompt-improver context, structured return\n69: \n70: Reply format: \"A, D, A, A\" or \"my prompt text here, B, A, A, B\"\n71: ```\n72: \n73: Reply-format rules: markdown dashes for bullets (never emoji bullets); each bullet on its own line; bold headers followed by content; no emojis in questions; defaults shown in brackets.\n74: \n75: ### Auto Fail-Fast Display\n76: \n77: When `:auto` is selected and `prompt_input` cannot be resolved from `$ARGUMENTS` or the pre-bound block:\n78: \n79: ```\n80: No prompt or topic was provided. /prompt:improve never infers prompt text\n81: from open files, screenshots, or conversation history.\n82: Re-run with the prompt inline, e.g. /prompt:improve \"your prompt here\" :auto\n83: \n84: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"prompt_input required and not provided\"\n85: ```\n86: \n87: ## 2. Dashboard / Checkpoint Layout\n88: \n89: Confirm-mode pauses reuse these templates.\n90: \n91: Checklist checkpoint (confirm mode, after the checklist pass):\n92: \n93: ```\n94: Checklist — [n] present, [n] absent, [n] not needed\n95: Shape: [default skeleton | preset name and reason]\n96: \n97: Continue to the draft, or revise the checklist? (continue / revise)\n98: ```\n99: \n100: Error recovery:\n101: \n102: | Situation | Response |\n103: |---|---|\n104: | No prompt provided | \"I need a prompt or request to enhance. What would you like me to improve?\" |\n105: | Ambiguous intent | Improve the existing prompt by default and list \"treated as an improvement, not a new prompt\" as open item 1 |\n106: | Invalid command | \"Available modes: $text, $improve, $refine, $short, $json, $yaml, $raw\" |\n107: | Pasted content, no context | Run a standard improvement and list the assumed goal as open item 1 |\n108: | Two mode commands | \"You used both [$a] and [$b]. Which mode do you want?\" |\n109: \n110: Questions: at most one, and only when there is no prompt and no task or two mode commands conflict; raw mode asks none. Every other gap gets a stated default, listed as a numbered open item after the prompt.\n111: \n112: ## 3. Results Display\n113: \n114: ### Success\n115: \n116: ```\n117: Enhanced Prompt ([FRAMEWORK] Framework):\n118: ─────────────────────────────────\n119: [Enhanced prompt, formatted per resolved mode: markdown default, JSON, or YAML]\n120: ─────────────────────────────────\n121: Transparency Report:\n122:   Framework: [default skeleton | preset name]\n123:   Mode: $[MODE] | Effort: [quick|standard|thorough]\n124:   Dispatch: [INLINE|AGENT]\n125:   Checklist: [N present, N added, N not needed]\n126:   Quick test: [ran: summary | NOT RUN]\n127:   CLEAR Score: [TOTAL]/50\n128:     C: [X]/10 | L: [X]/10 | E: [X]/15 | A: [X]/10 | R: [X]/5\n129:   Open items: [numbered list or None]\n130:   Changes: Added [..] | Changed [..] | Removed [..] | Skipped [..]\n131: \n132: [If saved] Saved to: [path]\n133: \n134: STATUS=OK SCORE=[N]/50 FRAMEWORK=[NAME][ SAVED=[path]]\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ### Failure\n138: \n139: ```\n140: [One-line reason.]\n141: \n142: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[specific message]\"\n143: ```\n144: \n145: Standard failure messages:\n146: - Skill missing: `sk-prompt skill not found at .skilled/skills/sk-prompt/SKILL.md`\n147: - CLEAR below threshold after 3 iterations: `CLEAR score below threshold after 3 iterations: [SCORE]/50`\n148: - User cancels: emit `STATUS=CANCELLED`\n149: \n150: ## 4. Next-Step Suggestions\n151: \n152: | Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n153: |-----------|-------------------|--------|\n154: | Enhanced prompt should become a skill | `/create:skill` | Scaffold an OpenCode skill from the prompt |\n155: | Prompt-engineering patterns worth documenting | `/create:readme` | Package the results as a documentation artifact |\n156: \n157: End interactive presentations with a single next-step prompt.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt, lines 1-157\n1: # Prompt Improve Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: Presentation source of truth for `/prompt:improve`. The router owns mode selection and asset loading. Workflow YAML owns execution. This file owns visible prompts, dashboard layout, and result displays.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: For `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt is the first visible response. Ask all applicable questions once, then wait. Never split them across multiple prompts.\n8: \n9: For `:auto`, do not show the consolidated prompt by default. Resolve setup through the auto-resolution table below and ask targeted questions only for fields that cannot be defaulted (Tier 2).\n10: \n11: ### Auto Pre-Bound Setup Answers\n12: \n13: Accept one optional marker block in the prompt body before applying defaults.\n14: \n15: ```yaml\n16: PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:\n17:   prompt_input: Help users understand our API authentication flow\n18:   enhancement_mode: auto\n19:   save_choice: D\n20:   save_path: \"\"\n21:   execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS\n22:   dispatch_mode: INLINE\n23: ```\n24: \n25: Unknown fields warn. Malformed lines are parse errors. Marker values override flags; omitted fields fall back to defaults.\n26: \n27: ### Auto Resolution Table\n28: \n29: | Field | Required | Default | Tier 2 (targeted-ask when) |\n30: |-------|----------|---------|----------------------------|\n31: | `prompt_input` | Yes | none | Never inferred — fail fast if missing (see Auto Fail-Fast Display) |\n32: | `enhancement_mode` | Yes | `auto` (detect from content) | No |\n33: | `save_choice` | Yes | `D` (keep in conversation only) | Yes, when the user's request implies persisting a prompt library |\n34: | `save_path` | No | none unless `save_choice` is A/B/C | No |\n35: | `execution_mode` | Yes | `AUTONOMOUS` under `:auto` | No |\n36: | `dispatch_mode` | Yes | `AGENT` when `--agent` or resolved complexity `>= 7/10`, else `INLINE` | No |\n37: \n38: ### Consolidated Prompt Template\n39: \n40: Include only the questions whose fields are still unresolved after parsing `$ARGUMENTS`. Ask them together in one turn, through the question tool that `.skilled/repo-rules/communication-handoff.md` §5 names for your runtime. Each question below becomes one tool question with its lettered options as the choices, and a free-text item such as a name or a path is answered through the tool's own free-text option. When the tool caps how many questions one call holds, make consecutive calls in the same turn. Only where §5 names no tool for this session, print the form below as text. Do not split these questions across turns.\n41: \n42: ```\n43: Before proceeding, please answer:\n44: \n45: Q0. Prompt Input (if not provided in command):\n46:     What prompt would you like to create or improve?\n47:     (paste prompt text, describe a topic, or specify a goal)\n48: \n49: Q1. Enhancement Mode (if no $mode prefix detected):\n50:     A) Auto-detect from content (Recommended)\n51:     B) $improve — Standard enhancement (all ten checklist rows)\n52:     C) $short — Quick refinement (four checklist rows)\n53:     D) $refine — Maximum optimization (all rows plus the quick test)\n54:     E) $raw — No checklist, format only\n55: \n56: Q2. Save Location (required):\n57:     A) Save to existing spec folder: [list if found]\n58:     B) Save to new spec folder\n59:     C) Save to specific path (inside the .opencode/specs/ tree)\n60:     D) Skip — keep in conversation only\n61: \n62: Q3. Execution Mode (if no :auto/:confirm suffix):\n63:     A) Autonomous — run end-to-end (Recommended)\n64:     B) Interactive — confirm after the checklist, the draft and the screen\n65: \n66: Q4. Dispatch Mode (if not auto-selected):\n67:     A) Inline skill — direct, in-context (default)\n68:     B) Agent — fresh @prompt-improver context, structured return\n69: \n70: Reply format: \"A, D, A, A\" or \"my prompt text here, B, A, A, B\"\n71: ```\n72: \n73: Reply-format rules: markdown dashes for bullets (never emoji bullets); each bullet on its own line; bold headers followed by content; no emojis in questions; defaults shown in brackets.\n74: \n75: ### Auto Fail-Fast Display\n76: \n77: When `:auto` is selected and `prompt_input` cannot be resolved from `$ARGUMENTS` or the pre-bound block:\n78: \n79: ```\n80: No prompt or topic was provided. /prompt:improve never infers prompt text\n81: from open files, screenshots, or conversation history.\n82: Re-run with the prompt inline, e.g. /prompt:improve \"your prompt here\" :auto\n83: \n84: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"prompt_input required and not provided\"\n85: ```\n86: \n87: ## 2. Dashboard / Checkpoint Layout\n88: \n89: Confirm-mode pauses reuse these templates.\n90: \n91: Checklist checkpoint (confirm mode, after the checklist pass):\n92: \n93: ```\n94: Checklist — [n] present, [n] absent, [n] not needed\n95: Shape: [default skeleton | preset name and reason]\n96: \n97: Continue to the draft, or revise the checklist? (continue / revise)\n98: ```\n99: \n100: Error recovery:\n101: \n102: | Situation | Response |\n103: |---|---|\n104: | No prompt provided | \"I need a prompt or request to enhance. What would you like me to improve?\" |\n105: | Ambiguous intent | Improve the existing prompt by default and list \"treated as an improvement, not a new prompt\" as open item 1 |\n106: | Invalid command | \"Available modes: $text, $improve, $refine, $short, $json, $yaml, $raw\" |\n107: | Pasted content, no context | Run a standard improvement and list the assumed goal as open item 1 |\n108: | Two mode commands | \"You used both [$a] and [$b]. Which mode do you want?\" |\n109: \n110: Questions: at most one, and only when there is no prompt and no task or two mode commands conflict; raw mode asks none. Every other gap gets a stated default, listed as a numbered open item after the prompt.\n111: \n112: ## 3. Results Display\n113: \n114: ### Success\n115: \n116: ```\n117: Enhanced Prompt ([FRAMEWORK] Framework):\n118: ─────────────────────────────────\n119: [Enhanced prompt, formatted per resolved mode: markdown default, JSON, or YAML]\n120: ─────────────────────────────────\n121: Transparency Report:\n122:   Framework: [default skeleton | preset name]\n123:   Mode: $[MODE] | Effort: [quick|standard|thorough]\n124:   Dispatch: [INLINE|AGENT]\n125:   Checklist: [N present, N added, N not needed]\n126:   Quick test: [ran: summary | NOT RUN]\n127:   CLEAR Score: [TOTAL]/50\n128:     C: [X]/10 | L: [X]/10 | E: [X]/15 | A: [X]/10 | R: [X]/5\n129:   Open items: [numbered list or None]\n130:   Changes: Added [..] | Changed [..] | Removed [..] | Skipped [..]\n131: \n132: [If saved] Saved to: [path]\n133: \n134: STATUS=OK SCORE=[N]/50 FRAMEWORK=[NAME][ SAVED=[path]]\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ### Failure\n138: \n139: ```\n140: [One-line reason.]\n141: \n142: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[specific message]\"\n143: ```\n144: \n145: Standard failure messages:\n146: - Skill missing: `sk-prompt skill not found at .skilled/skills/sk-prompt/SKILL.md`\n147: - CLEAR below threshold after 3 iterations: `CLEAR score below threshold after 3 iterations: [SCORE]/50`\n148: - User cancels: emit `STATUS=CANCELLED`\n149: \n150: ## 4. Next-Step Suggestions\n151: \n152: | Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n153: |-----------|-------------------|--------|\n154: | Enhanced prompt should become a skill | `/create:skill` | Scaffold an OpenCode skill from the prompt |\n155: | Prompt-engineering patterns worth documenting | `/create:readme` | Package the results as a documentation artifact |\n156: \n157: End interactive presentations with a single next-step prompt."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582807272,"end":1794582807747}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582807753,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5788450001GVXR6z5cpj6z63","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d5787c5c001akopz7L6rps5c6","type":"tool","id":"call_01_ET_Yss3pZ7VsCWC3OTFWFzX3164","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs, lines 1-465\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Command Catalog Mirror Check\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // Read-only /doctor diagnostic for command-catalog and command-metadata drift.\n8: //\n9: // WHY THIS EXISTS: a command's own frontmatter is the only place its identity is\n10: // stated once. Everything else that names commands is a copy — the repo-wide\n11: // index at .skilled/commands/README.txt, the per-family indexes beside it, and\n12: // the command-metadata.json each hub keeps so the skill advisor can route to a\n13: // command it owns. Adding, renaming or deleting a command updates the file and\n14: // none of the copies, and nothing notices: the runtime still dispatches, the\n15: // advisor still routes what it knows about, and only a reader who trusts an\n16: // index is misled. This check makes that omission loud.\n17: //\n18: // It compares copies against the frontmatter tree, never a copy against a copy,\n19: // so it stays a guard rather than a second generator. Generating the indexes was\n20: // considered and rejected: the hub metadata covers only the commands whose hubs\n21: // route them, well short of the whole tree, and is itself hand-kept, so deriving\n22: // one copy from another would launder drift instead of reporting it.\n23: //\n24: // Two tiers, because two kinds of disagreement are not the same failure:\n25: //   - Structural (drives exit status). Coverage, identity, counts and resolvable\n26: //     resources. A command missing from an index, an index naming a command that\n27: //     no longer exists, a stale or missing group row, a metadata entry pointing\n28: //     at nothing. These break a reader or a router.\n29: //   - Prose (reported, exit 0 unless --strict). The description and argumentHint\n30: //     a hub copies out of frontmatter. A hub legitimately phrases a routing\n31: //     description its own way, and the metadata convention appends a pre-bound\n32: //     setup annotation the frontmatter often omits, so a verbatim mismatch is\n33: //     worth seeing without being worth failing a diagnostic over.\n34: //\n35: // Never writes; a /doctor run is read-only by contract.\n36: // Exit 0 when every copy covers the tree, 1 on drift, 2 on checker error (bad\n37: // arguments, a missing tree, or any unexpected throw), always with a STATUS= line.\n38: //\n39: // Usage: command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--strict] [--check]\n40: //   --root   check a copy of the tree instead of this repository, so a\n41: //            deliberate staleness can be proven without editing the real one.\n42: //   --strict promote prose divergence from a warning to drift.\n43: //   --check  accepted as a no-op, because this checker is read-only either way\n44: //            and the sibling mirror checkers take the flag.\n45: \n46: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n47: // 1. IMPORTS\n48: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: \n50: const fs = require('node:fs');\n51: const path = require('node:path');\n52: \n53: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: // 2. CONSTANTS\n55: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: \n57: const DEFAULT_REPO = path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../..');\n58: \n59: // Directories under .skilled/commands/ that hold support files rather than\n60: // commands. Anything else with .md files in it is a command namespace.\n61: const NON_NAMESPACE_DIRS = new Set(['assets', 'scripts']);\n62: \n63: // Hubs keep their command-metadata beside their SKILL.md. Only hubs that own\n64: // commands carry entries; a hub with none carries an empty array.\n65: const METADATA_GLOB_ROOT = '.skilled/skills';\n66: \n67: // The group table names root utilities under this label rather than a folder.\n68: const ROOT_GROUP = 'root';\n69: \n70: // A slash-command id: /name for a root utility, /family:name for a namespaced\n71: // one. The same grammar the metadata schema enforces.\n72: const COMMAND_ID_RE = /^\\/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(:[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)?$/;\n73: \n74: // Namespaced command ids mentioned in prose. Root-form ids (/goal-opencode) are not\n75: // scanned for orphans: a bare slash-word is too easily a path or a fragment, and\n76: // a false orphan trains the reader to ignore this output.\n77: const NAMESPACED_MENTION_RE = /\\/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*:[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/g;\n78: \n79: const BACKTICK_SPAN_RE = /`([^`]+)`/g;\n80: \n81: // The metadata convention appends this annotation to an argument hint whose\n82: // :auto mode accepts pre-bound setup answers; the frontmatter carries it only on\n83: // some commands. The two surfaces disagree systematically rather than by drift,\n84: // so the grammar is compared without it.\n85: const PREBOUND_ANNOTATION_RE = /\\s*\\(:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS[^)]*\\)\\s*$/;\n86: \n87: // Width of the catalog or metadata label column in the report.\n88: const LABEL_WIDTH = 34;\n89: \n90: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n91: // 3. HELPERS\n92: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n93: \n94: function fail(message) {\n95:   console.error(`STATUS=ERROR command-catalog-mirror: ${message}`);\n96:   process.exit(2);\n97: }\n98: \n99: function parseArgs(argv) {\n100:   const opts = { root: DEFAULT_REPO, strict: false };\n101:   for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {\n102:     if (argv[i] === '--strict') opts.strict = true;\n103:     // Every run here is a check, so the flag its siblings require names no other\n104:     // mode; refusing it would fail a valid shared invocation.\n105:     else if (argv[i] === '--check') continue;\n106:     else if (argv[i] === '--root') {\n107:       const next = argv[++i];\n108:       if (!next) fail('--root needs a directory');\n109:       opts.root = path.resolve(next);\n110:     } else fail(`unknown argument: ${argv[i]}`);\n111:   }\n112:   return opts;\n113: }\n114: \n115: function tableCells(line) {\n116:   return line.trim().replace(/^\\|/, '').replace(/\\|$/, '').split('|').map((c) => c.trim());\n117: }\n118: \n119: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n120: // 4. THE TREE OF RECORD\n121: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n122: \n123: function readFrontmatter(file) {\n124:   const text = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n125:   const block = text.match(/^---\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\n---/);\n126:   if (!block) return {};\n127:   const fields = {};\n128:   for (const line of block[1].split('\\n')) {\n129:     const kv = line.match(/^([A-Za-z][A-Za-z-]*):\\s*(.*)$/);\n130:     if (!kv) continue;\n131:     let value = kv[2].trim();\n132:     const quoted = (value.startsWith('\"') && value.endsWith('\"')) ||\n133:       (value.startsWith(\"'\") && value.endsWith(\"'\"));\n134:     if (quoted && value.length >= 2) value = value.slice(1, -1);\n135:     fields[kv[1]] = value;\n136:   }\n137:   return fields;\n138: }\n139: \n140: // Every shipped command, from the files themselves.\n141: function readCommandTree(commandsDir) {\n142:   const commands = [];\n143:   for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(commandsDir).sort()) {\n144:     // A local-* command or namespace is private to one checkout and git-ignored,\n145:     // so no tracked catalog may list it and its absence from one is not drift.\n146:     if (entry.startsWith('local-')) continue;\n147:     const abs = path.join(commandsDir, entry);\n148:     if (fs.statSync(abs).isDirectory()) {\n149:       if (NON_NAMESPACE_DIRS.has(entry)) continue;\n150:       for (const file of fs.readdirSync(abs).sort()) {\n151:         if (!file.endsWith('.md')) continue;\n152:         const name = file.slice(0, -3);\n153:         commands.push({\n154:           id: `/${entry}:${name}`,\n155:           ns: entry,\n156:           name,\n157:           abs: path.join(abs, file),\n158:           rel: `${entry}/${file}`,\n159:           frontmatter: readFrontmatter(path.join(abs, file)),\n160:         });\n161:       }\n162:     } else if (entry.endsWith('.md')) {\n163:       const name = entry.slice(0, -3);\n164:       commands.push({\n165:         id: `/${name}`,\n166:         ns: null,\n167:         name,\n168:         abs,\n169:         rel: entry,\n170:         frontmatter: readFrontmatter(abs),\n171:       });\n172:     }\n173:   }\n174:   return commands;\n175: }\n176: \n177: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n178: // 5. CATALOGS\n179: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n180: \n181: // Coverage is judged per table row, never over the whole document and never by\n182: // substring. A usage example further down mentions ids in passing, a group row's\n183: // description names the commands of its group, and one id can be the prefix of\n184: // another (/create:skill inside /create:skill-parent). Any of those lets a\n185: // deleted row hide, which is precisely the staleness worth catching. So a row\n186: // names the command its first backticked span opens with, compared exactly.\n187: //\n188: // A row may instead name the command by its backing file, as any backticked span\n189: // equal to the file path. The doctor router is the reason the fallback exists:\n190: // a router row can name a placeholder form, `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`.\n191: function catalogEntries(text) {\n192:   const ids = new Set();\n193:   const paths = new Set();\n194:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n195:     if (!/^\\s*\\|/.test(line)) continue;\n196:     const spans = [...line.matchAll(BACKTICK_SPAN_RE)].map((m) => m[1].trim());\n197:     if (spans.length === 0) continue;\n198:     const firstWord = spans[0].split(/\\s+/)[0];\n199:     if (COMMAND_ID_RE.test(firstWord)) ids.add(firstWord);\n200:     for (const span of spans) paths.add(span);\n201:   }\n202:   return { ids, paths };\n203: }\n204: \n205: function catalogNames(entries, command) {\n206:   return entries.ids.has(command.id) || entries.paths.has(command.rel);\n207: }\n208: \n209: function findCatalogs(commandsDir, namespaces) {\n210:   const catalogs = [];\n211:   const repoWide = path.join(commandsDir, 'README.txt');\n212:   if (fs.existsSync(repoWide)) {\n213:     catalogs.push({ label: 'commands/README.txt', abs: repoWide, scope: null });\n214:   }\n215:   for (const ns of namespaces) {\n216:     const abs = path.join(commandsDir, ns, 'README.txt');\n217:     if (fs.existsSync(abs)) {\n218:       catalogs.push({ label: `commands/${ns}/README.txt`, abs, scope: ns });\n219:     }\n220:   }\n221:   return catalogs;\n222: }\n223: \n224: // The repo-wide index opens with a group table carrying a command count per\n225: // group. The count is the claim most likely to rot, and the index says so itself.\n226: function groupCounts(text) {\n227:   const counts = new Map();\n228:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n229:     if (!/^\\s*\\|/.test(line)) continue;\n230:     const cells = tableCells(line);\n231:     if (cells.length < 3) continue;\n232:     const group = cells[0].match(/^\\*\\*([a-z][a-z0-9-]*)\\*\\*$/);\n233:     const count = cells[2].match(/^\\d+$/);\n234:     if (group && count) counts.set(group[1], Number(count[0]));\n235:   }\n236:   return counts;\n237: }\n238: \n239: function commandsInGroup(commands, group) {\n240:   return group === ROOT_GROUP\n241:     ? commands.filter((c) => c.ns === null)\n242:     : commands.filter((c) => c.ns === group);\n243: }\n244: \n245: // The group table is checked both ways: a row whose folder is gone, a count\n246: // that no longer matches, and a namespace (or the root) whose commands have no\n247: // row at all, the omission a newly added family produces.\n248: function checkGroupTable(text, commands, namespaces) {\n249:   const problems = [];\n250:   const counts = groupCounts(text);\n251:   for (const [group, claimed] of counts) {\n252:     const actual = commandsInGroup(commands, group).length;\n253:     if (actual === 0 && group !== ROOT_GROUP) {\n254:       problems.push(`group table lists '${group}' but no such command folder`);\n255:     } else if (actual !== claimed) {\n256:       problems.push(`group '${group}' count says ${claimed}, folder holds ${actual}`);\n257:     }\n258:   }\n259:   const groups = [...namespaces].sort();\n260:   if (commandsInGroup(commands, ROOT_GROUP).length > 0) groups.push(ROOT_GROUP);\n261:   for (const group of groups) {\n262:     if (counts.has(group)) continue;\n263:     const actual = commandsInGroup(commands, group).length;\n264:     problems.push(`'${group}' has ${actual} command(s) but no group-table row`);\n265:   }\n266:   return problems;\n267: }\n268: \n269: function checkCatalog(catalog, commands, namespaces) {\n270:   const text = fs.readFileSync(catalog.abs, 'utf8');\n271:   const entries = catalogEntries(text);\n272:   const inScope = catalog.scope === null\n273:     ? commands\n274:     : commands.filter((c) => c.ns === catalog.scope);\n275:   const problems = [];\n276: \n277:   const unlisted = inScope.filter((command) => !catalogNames(entries, command));\n278:   for (const command of unlisted) problems.push(`${command.id} not listed`);\n279: \n280:   // An id in the catalog with no file behind it is drift the other way: the\n281:   // index keeps offering a command the tree no longer defines.\n282:   const known = new Set(commands.map((c) => c.id));\n283:   const scanned = new Set();\n284:   for (const mention of text.match(NAMESPACED_MENTION_RE) || []) {\n285:     if (scanned.has(mention)) continue;\n286:     scanned.add(mention);\n287:     const ns = mention.slice(1).split(':')[0];\n288:     if (catalog.scope !== null && ns !== catalog.scope) continue;\n289:     if (!namespaces.has(ns)) continue;\n290:     if (!known.has(mention)) problems.push(`${mention} listed but no such command file`);\n291:   }\n292: \n293:   if (catalog.scope === null) problems.push(...checkGroupTable(text, commands, namespaces));\n294: \n295:   return { covered: inScope.length - unlisted.length, total: inScope.length, problems };\n296: }\n297: \n298: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n299: // 6. HUB COMMAND METADATA\n300: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n301: \n302: function findMetadataFiles(repo) {\n303:   const skillsDir = path.join(repo, METADATA_GLOB_ROOT);\n304:   if (!fs.existsSync(skillsDir)) return [];\n305:   const found = [];\n306:   for (const skill of fs.readdirSync(skillsDir).sort()) {\n307:     // A local-* skill is private to one checkout, so its metadata never feeds a tracked catalog.\n308:     if (skill.startsWith('local-')) continue;\n309:     const abs = path.join(skillsDir, skill, 'command-metadata.json');\n310:     if (fs.existsSync(abs)) found.push({ label: `${skill}/command-metadata.json`, abs, skill });\n311:   }\n312:   return found;\n313: }\n314: \n315: function isPlainObject(value) {\n316:   return value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n317: }\n318: \n319: function checkEntry(entry, command, repo, problems, warnings) {\n320:   const id = command.id;\n321:   if (entry.choreography !== undefined && !Array.isArray(entry.choreography)) {\n322:     problems.push(`${id} choreography is not an array`);\n323:   }\n324:   for (const step of Array.isArray(entry.choreography) ? entry.choreography : []) {\n325:     if (!step || typeof step.resource !== 'string') continue;\n326:     if (!fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, step.resource))) {\n327:       problems.push(`${id} loads a resource that does not exist: ${step.resource}`);\n328:     }\n329:   }\n330: \n331:   const description = command.frontmatter.description || '';\n332:   if ((entry.description || '') !== description) {\n333:     warnings.push(`${id} description differs from frontmatter`);\n334:   }\n335:   const hint = (command.frontmatter['argument-hint'] || '').replace(PREBOUND_ANNOTATION_RE, '');\n336:   const claimed = (entry.argumentHint || '').replace(PREBOUND_ANNOTATION_RE, '');\n337:   if (claimed !== hint) {\n338:     warnings.push(`${id} argumentHint differs from frontmatter`);\n339:   }\n340: }\n341: \n342: function checkMetadata(meta, commands, repo) {\n343:   let entries;\n344:   try {\n345:     entries = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(meta.abs, 'utf8'));\n346:   } catch (err) {\n347:     return { problems: [`unparseable: ${err.message}`], warnings: [], entries: 0 };\n348:   }\n349:   if (!Array.isArray(entries)) return { problems: ['not an array'], warnings: [], entries: 0 };\n350: \n351:   const byId = new Map(commands.map((c) => [c.id, c]));\n352:   const problems = [];\n353:   const warnings = [];\n354:   const claimedNamespaces = new Set();\n355:   const declared = new Set();\n356: \n357:   entries.forEach((entry, index) => {\n358:     // A null or scalar entry carries no command to check; it is still drift,\n359:     // because the file no longer has the shape the advisor reads.\n360:     if (!isPlainObject(entry)) {\n361:       problems.push(`entry ${index + 1} is not an object`);\n362:       return;\n363:     }\n364:     const id = typeof entry.command === 'string' ? entry.command : '(unnamed entry)';\n365:     if (!COMMAND_ID_RE.test(id)) {\n366:       problems.push(`${id} is not a slash-command id`);\n367:       return;\n368:     }\n369:     declared.add(id);\n370:     const command = byId.get(id);\n371:     if (!command) {\n372:       problems.push(`${id} has an entry but no command file`);\n373:       return;\n374:     }\n375:     if (command.ns) claimedNamespaces.add(command.ns);\n376:     checkEntry(entry, command, repo, problems, warnings);\n377:   });\n378: \n379:   // A hub that speaks for a namespace speaks for all of it. Half a namespace is\n380:   // how a newly added command goes unrouted while the file sits happily on disk.\n381:   for (const ns of claimedNamespaces) {\n382:     for (const command of commands.filter((c) => c.ns === ns)) {\n383:       if (!declared.has(command.id)) {\n384:         problems.push(`${command.id} has no entry, though this hub covers the rest of ${ns}/`);\n385:       }\n386:     }\n387:   }\n388: \n389:   return { problems, warnings, entries: entries.length };\n390: }\n391: \n392: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n393: // 7. REPORT\n394: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n395: \n396: function main() {\n397:   const opts = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n398:   const commandsDir = path.join(opts.root, '.skilled/commands');\n399:   if (!fs.existsSync(commandsDir)) fail(`commands directory not found: ${commandsDir}`);\n400: \n401:   const commands = readCommandTree(commandsDir);\n402:   if (commands.length === 0) fail(`no command files under ${commandsDir}`);\n403:   const namespaces = new Set(commands.map((c) => c.ns).filter(Boolean));\n404: \n405:   const drift = [];\n406:   const prose = [];\n407: \n408:   console.log('\\n/doctor command-catalog-mirror — read-only coverage check');\n409:   console.log(`canonical: .skilled/commands frontmatter (${commands.length} commands)\\n`);\n410: \n411:   const catalogs = findCatalogs(commandsDir, [...namespaces].sort());\n412:   if (catalogs.length === 0) {\n413:     drift.push('catalog: no README.txt index found under .skilled/commands');\n414:   }\n415:   for (const catalog of catalogs) {\n416:     const result = checkCatalog(catalog, commands, namespaces);\n417:     const mark = result.problems.length === 0 ? 'OK  ' : 'DRIFT';\n418:     const label = catalog.label.padEnd(LABEL_WIDTH);\n419:     console.log(`  ${mark} ${label} ${result.covered}/${result.total} listed`);\n420:     for (const p of result.problems) {\n421:       console.log(`         - ${p}`);\n422:       drift.push(`${catalog.label}: ${p}`);\n423:     }\n424:   }\n425: \n426:   for (const meta of findMetadataFiles(opts.root)) {\n427:     const result = checkMetadata(meta, commands, opts.root);\n428:     if (result.entries === 0 && result.problems.length === 0) continue;\n429:     const mark = result.problems.length === 0 ? 'OK  ' : 'DRIFT';\n430:     const noun = result.entries === 1 ? 'entry' : 'entries';\n431:     console.log(`  ${mark} ${meta.label.padEnd(LABEL_WIDTH)} ${result.entries} ${noun}`);\n432:     for (const p of result.problems) {\n433:       console.log(`         - ${p}`);\n434:       drift.push(`${meta.label}: ${p}`);\n435:     }\n436:     for (const w of result.warnings) {\n437:       console.log(`         ? ${w}`);\n438:       prose.push(`${meta.label}: ${w}`);\n439:     }\n440:   }\n441: \n442:   if (prose.length > 0 && !opts.strict) {\n443:     console.log(`\\n  ${prose.length} prose divergence(s) reported above; --strict fails on them.`);\n444:   }\n445: \n446:   const failing = opts.strict ? drift.length + prose.length : drift.length;\n447:   if (failing > 0) {\n448:     console.log(`\\nSTATUS=DRIFT command-catalog-mirror: ${failing} issue(s)`);\n449:     console.log('Repair: the command file\\'s frontmatter is the source. Update the index row, '\n450:       + 'the group row or count, or the hub metadata entry to match it — '\n451:       + 'never the other way round.\\n');\n452:     process.exit(1);\n453:   }\n454:   console.log('\\nSTATUS=OK command-catalog-mirror: '\n455:     + 'every catalog and hub metadata covers the command tree\\n');\n456:   process.exit(0);\n457: }\n458: \n459: // Any throw is the checker failing, never a drift verdict, so it must reach the\n460: // exit code the workflow maps to checker error rather than Node's default 1.\n461: try {\n462:   main();\n463: } catch (err) {\n464:   fail(`checker crashed: ${err && err.message ? err.message : String(err)}`);\n465: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs, lines 1-465\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Command Catalog Mirror Check\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // Read-only /doctor diagnostic for command-catalog and command-metadata drift.\n8: //\n9: // WHY THIS EXISTS: a command's own frontmatter is the only place its identity is\n10: // stated once. Everything else that names commands is a copy — the repo-wide\n11: // index at .skilled/commands/README.txt, the per-family indexes beside it, and\n12: // the command-metadata.json each hub keeps so the skill advisor can route to a\n13: // command it owns. Adding, renaming or deleting a command updates the file and\n14: // none of the copies, and nothing notices: the runtime still dispatches, the\n15: // advisor still routes what it knows about, and only a reader who trusts an\n16: // index is misled. This check makes that omission loud.\n17: //\n18: // It compares copies against the frontmatter tree, never a copy against a copy,\n19: // so it stays a guard rather than a second generator. Generating the indexes was\n20: // considered and rejected: the hub metadata covers only the commands whose hubs\n21: // route them, well short of the whole tree, and is itself hand-kept, so deriving\n22: // one copy from another would launder drift instead of reporting it.\n23: //\n24: // Two tiers, because two kinds of disagreement are not the same failure:\n25: //   - Structural (drives exit status). Coverage, identity, counts and resolvable\n26: //     resources. A command missing from an index, an index naming a command that\n27: //     no longer exists, a stale or missing group row, a metadata entry pointing\n28: //     at nothing. These break a reader or a router.\n29: //   - Prose (reported, exit 0 unless --strict). The description and argumentHint\n30: //     a hub copies out of frontmatter. A hub legitimately phrases a routing\n31: //     description its own way, and the metadata convention appends a pre-bound\n32: //     setup annotation the frontmatter often omits, so a verbatim mismatch is\n33: //     worth seeing without being worth failing a diagnostic over.\n34: //\n35: // Never writes; a /doctor run is read-only by contract.\n36: // Exit 0 when every copy covers the tree, 1 on drift, 2 on checker error (bad\n37: // arguments, a missing tree, or any unexpected throw), always with a STATUS= line.\n38: //\n39: // Usage: command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--strict] [--check]\n40: //   --root   check a copy of the tree instead of this repository, so a\n41: //            deliberate staleness can be proven without editing the real one.\n42: //   --strict promote prose divergence from a warning to drift.\n43: //   --check  accepted as a no-op, because this checker is read-only either way\n44: //            and the sibling mirror checkers take the flag.\n45: \n46: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n47: // 1. IMPORTS\n48: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n49: \n50: const fs = require('node:fs');\n51: const path = require('node:path');\n52: \n53: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: // 2. CONSTANTS\n55: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: \n57: const DEFAULT_REPO = path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../..');\n58: \n59: // Directories under .skilled/commands/ that hold support files rather than\n60: // commands. Anything else with .md files in it is a command namespace.\n61: const NON_NAMESPACE_DIRS = new Set(['assets', 'scripts']);\n62: \n63: // Hubs keep their command-metadata beside their SKILL.md. Only hubs that own\n64: // commands carry entries; a hub with none carries an empty array.\n65: const METADATA_GLOB_ROOT = '.skilled/skills';\n66: \n67: // The group table names root utilities under this label rather than a folder.\n68: const ROOT_GROUP = 'root';\n69: \n70: // A slash-command id: /name for a root utility, /family:name for a namespaced\n71: // one. The same grammar the metadata schema enforces.\n72: const COMMAND_ID_RE = /^\\/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(:[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)?$/;\n73: \n74: // Namespaced command ids mentioned in prose. Root-form ids (/goal-opencode) are not\n75: // scanned for orphans: a bare slash-word is too easily a path or a fragment, and\n76: // a false orphan trains the reader to ignore this output.\n77: const NAMESPACED_MENTION_RE = /\\/[a-z][a-z0-9-]*:[a-z][a-z0-9-]*/g;\n78: \n79: const BACKTICK_SPAN_RE = /`([^`]+)`/g;\n80: \n81: // The metadata convention appends this annotation to an argument hint whose\n82: // :auto mode accepts pre-bound setup answers; the frontmatter carries it only on\n83: // some commands. The two surfaces disagree systematically rather than by drift,\n84: // so the grammar is compared without it.\n85: const PREBOUND_ANNOTATION_RE = /\\s*\\(:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS[^)]*\\)\\s*$/;\n86: \n87: // Width of the catalog or metadata label column in the report.\n88: const LABEL_WIDTH = 34;\n89: \n90: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n91: // 3. HELPERS\n92: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n93: \n94: function fail(message) {\n95:   console.error(`STATUS=ERROR command-catalog-mirror: ${message}`);\n96:   process.exit(2);\n97: }\n98: \n99: function parseArgs(argv) {\n100:   const opts = { root: DEFAULT_REPO, strict: false };\n101:   for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {\n102:     if (argv[i] === '--strict') opts.strict = true;\n103:     // Every run here is a check, so the flag its siblings require names no other\n104:     // mode; refusing it would fail a valid shared invocation.\n105:     else if (argv[i] === '--check') continue;\n106:     else if (argv[i] === '--root') {\n107:       const next = argv[++i];\n108:       if (!next) fail('--root needs a directory');\n109:       opts.root = path.resolve(next);\n110:     } else fail(`unknown argument: ${argv[i]}`);\n111:   }\n112:   return opts;\n113: }\n114: \n115: function tableCells(line) {\n116:   return line.trim().replace(/^\\|/, '').replace(/\\|$/, '').split('|').map((c) => c.trim());\n117: }\n118: \n119: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n120: // 4. THE TREE OF RECORD\n121: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n122: \n123: function readFrontmatter(file) {\n124:   const text = fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n125:   const block = text.match(/^---\\n([\\s\\S]*?)\\n---/);\n126:   if (!block) return {};\n127:   const fields = {};\n128:   for (const line of block[1].split('\\n')) {\n129:     const kv = line.match(/^([A-Za-z][A-Za-z-]*):\\s*(.*)$/);\n130:     if (!kv) continue;\n131:     let value = kv[2].trim();\n132:     const quoted = (value.startsWith('\"') && value.endsWith('\"')) ||\n133:       (value.startsWith(\"'\") && value.endsWith(\"'\"));\n134:     if (quoted && value.length >= 2) value = value.slice(1, -1);\n135:     fields[kv[1]] = value;\n136:   }\n137:   return fields;\n138: }\n139: \n140: // Every shipped command, from the files themselves.\n141: function readCommandTree(commandsDir) {\n142:   const commands = [];\n143:   for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(commandsDir).sort()) {\n144:     // A local-* command or namespace is private to one checkout and git-ignored,\n145:     // so no tracked catalog may list it and its absence from one is not drift.\n146:     if (entry.startsWith('local-')) continue;\n147:     const abs = path.join(commandsDir, entry);\n148:     if (fs.statSync(abs).isDirectory()) {\n149:       if (NON_NAMESPACE_DIRS.has(entry)) continue;\n150:       for (const file of fs.readdirSync(abs).sort()) {\n151:         if (!file.endsWith('.md')) continue;\n152:         const name = file.slice(0, -3);\n153:         commands.push({\n154:           id: `/${entry}:${name}`,\n155:           ns: entry,\n156:           name,\n157:           abs: path.join(abs, file),\n158:           rel: `${entry}/${file}`,\n159:           frontmatter: readFrontmatter(path.join(abs, file)),\n160:         });\n161:       }\n162:     } else if (entry.endsWith('.md')) {\n163:       const name = entry.slice(0, -3);\n164:       commands.push({\n165:         id: `/${name}`,\n166:         ns: null,\n167:         name,\n168:         abs,\n169:         rel: entry,\n170:         frontmatter: readFrontmatter(abs),\n171:       });\n172:     }\n173:   }\n174:   return commands;\n175: }\n176: \n177: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n178: // 5. CATALOGS\n179: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n180: \n181: // Coverage is judged per table row, never over the whole document and never by\n182: // substring. A usage example further down mentions ids in passing, a group row's\n183: // description names the commands of its group, and one id can be the prefix of\n184: // another (/create:skill inside /create:skill-parent). Any of those lets a\n185: // deleted row hide, which is precisely the staleness worth catching. So a row\n186: // names the command its first backticked span opens with, compared exactly.\n187: //\n188: // A row may instead name the command by its backing file, as any backticked span\n189: // equal to the file path. The doctor router is the reason the fallback exists:\n190: // a router row can name a placeholder form, `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`.\n191: function catalogEntries(text) {\n192:   const ids = new Set();\n193:   const paths = new Set();\n194:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n195:     if (!/^\\s*\\|/.test(line)) continue;\n196:     const spans = [...line.matchAll(BACKTICK_SPAN_RE)].map((m) => m[1].trim());\n197:     if (spans.length === 0) continue;\n198:     const firstWord = spans[0].split(/\\s+/)[0];\n199:     if (COMMAND_ID_RE.test(firstWord)) ids.add(firstWord);\n200:     for (const span of spans) paths.add(span);\n201:   }\n202:   return { ids, paths };\n203: }\n204: \n205: function catalogNames(entries, command) {\n206:   return entries.ids.has(command.id) || entries.paths.has(command.rel);\n207: }\n208: \n209: function findCatalogs(commandsDir, namespaces) {\n210:   const catalogs = [];\n211:   const repoWide = path.join(commandsDir, 'README.txt');\n212:   if (fs.existsSync(repoWide)) {\n213:     catalogs.push({ label: 'commands/README.txt', abs: repoWide, scope: null });\n214:   }\n215:   for (const ns of namespaces) {\n216:     const abs = path.join(commandsDir, ns, 'README.txt');\n217:     if (fs.existsSync(abs)) {\n218:       catalogs.push({ label: `commands/${ns}/README.txt`, abs, scope: ns });\n219:     }\n220:   }\n221:   return catalogs;\n222: }\n223: \n224: // The repo-wide index opens with a group table carrying a command count per\n225: // group. The count is the claim most likely to rot, and the index says so itself.\n226: function groupCounts(text) {\n227:   const counts = new Map();\n228:   for (const line of text.split('\\n')) {\n229:     if (!/^\\s*\\|/.test(line)) continue;\n230:     const cells = tableCells(line);\n231:     if (cells.length < 3) continue;\n232:     const group = cells[0].match(/^\\*\\*([a-z][a-z0-9-]*)\\*\\*$/);\n233:     const count = cells[2].match(/^\\d+$/);\n234:     if (group && count) counts.set(group[1], Number(count[0]));\n235:   }\n236:   return counts;\n237: }\n238: \n239: function commandsInGroup(commands, group) {\n240:   return group === ROOT_GROUP\n241:     ? commands.filter((c) => c.ns === null)\n242:     : commands.filter((c) => c.ns === group);\n243: }\n244: \n245: // The group table is checked both ways: a row whose folder is gone, a count\n246: // that no longer matches, and a namespace (or the root) whose commands have no\n247: // row at all, the omission a newly added family produces.\n248: function checkGroupTable(text, commands, namespaces) {\n249:   const problems = [];\n250:   const counts = groupCounts(text);\n251:   for (const [group, claimed] of counts) {\n252:     const actual = commandsInGroup(commands, group).length;\n253:     if (actual === 0 && group !== ROOT_GROUP) {\n254:       problems.push(`group table lists '${group}' but no such command folder`);\n255:     } else if (actual !== claimed) {\n256:       problems.push(`group '${group}' count says ${claimed}, folder holds ${actual}`);\n257:     }\n258:   }\n259:   const groups = [...namespaces].sort();\n260:   if (commandsInGroup(commands, ROOT_GROUP).length > 0) groups.push(ROOT_GROUP);\n261:   for (const group of groups) {\n262:     if (counts.has(group)) continue;\n263:     const actual = commandsInGroup(commands, group).length;\n264:     problems.push(`'${group}' has ${actual} command(s) but no group-table row`);\n265:   }\n266:   return problems;\n267: }\n268: \n269: function checkCatalog(catalog, commands, namespaces) {\n270:   const text = fs.readFileSync(catalog.abs, 'utf8');\n271:   const entries = catalogEntries(text);\n272:   const inScope = catalog.scope === null\n273:     ? commands\n274:     : commands.filter((c) => c.ns === catalog.scope);\n275:   const problems = [];\n276: \n277:   const unlisted = inScope.filter((command) => !catalogNames(entries, command));\n278:   for (const command of unlisted) problems.push(`${command.id} not listed`);\n279: \n280:   // An id in the catalog with no file behind it is drift the other way: the\n281:   // index keeps offering a command the tree no longer defines.\n282:   const known = new Set(commands.map((c) => c.id));\n283:   const scanned = new Set();\n284:   for (const mention of text.match(NAMESPACED_MENTION_RE) || []) {\n285:     if (scanned.has(mention)) continue;\n286:     scanned.add(mention);\n287:     const ns = mention.slice(1).split(':')[0];\n288:     if (catalog.scope !== null && ns !== catalog.scope) continue;\n289:     if (!namespaces.has(ns)) continue;\n290:     if (!known.has(mention)) problems.push(`${mention} listed but no such command file`);\n291:   }\n292: \n293:   if (catalog.scope === null) problems.push(...checkGroupTable(text, commands, namespaces));\n294: \n295:   return { covered: inScope.length - unlisted.length, total: inScope.length, problems };\n296: }\n297: \n298: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n299: // 6. HUB COMMAND METADATA\n300: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n301: \n302: function findMetadataFiles(repo) {\n303:   const skillsDir = path.join(repo, METADATA_GLOB_ROOT);\n304:   if (!fs.existsSync(skillsDir)) return [];\n305:   const found = [];\n306:   for (const skill of fs.readdirSync(skillsDir).sort()) {\n307:     // A local-* skill is private to one checkout, so its metadata never feeds a tracked catalog.\n308:     if (skill.startsWith('local-')) continue;\n309:     const abs = path.join(skillsDir, skill, 'command-metadata.json');\n310:     if (fs.existsSync(abs)) found.push({ label: `${skill}/command-metadata.json`, abs, skill });\n311:   }\n312:   return found;\n313: }\n314: \n315: function isPlainObject(value) {\n316:   return value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n317: }\n318: \n319: function checkEntry(entry, command, repo, problems, warnings) {\n320:   const id = command.id;\n321:   if (entry.choreography !== undefined && !Array.isArray(entry.choreography)) {\n322:     problems.push(`${id} choreography is not an array`);\n323:   }\n324:   for (const step of Array.isArray(entry.choreography) ? entry.choreography : []) {\n325:     if (!step || typeof step.resource !== 'string') continue;\n326:     if (!fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, step.resource))) {\n327:       problems.push(`${id} loads a resource that does not exist: ${step.resource}`);\n328:     }\n329:   }\n330: \n331:   const description = command.frontmatter.description || '';\n332:   if ((entry.description || '') !== description) {\n333:     warnings.push(`${id} description differs from frontmatter`);\n334:   }\n335:   const hint = (command.frontmatter['argument-hint'] || '').replace(PREBOUND_ANNOTATION_RE, '');\n336:   const claimed = (entry.argumentHint || '').replace(PREBOUND_ANNOTATION_RE, '');\n337:   if (claimed !== hint) {\n338:     warnings.push(`${id} argumentHint differs from frontmatter`);\n339:   }\n340: }\n341: \n342: function checkMetadata(meta, commands, repo) {\n343:   let entries;\n344:   try {\n345:     entries = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(meta.abs, 'utf8'));\n346:   } catch (err) {\n347:     return { problems: [`unparseable: ${err.message}`], warnings: [], entries: 0 };\n348:   }\n349:   if (!Array.isArray(entries)) return { problems: ['not an array'], warnings: [], entries: 0 };\n350: \n351:   const byId = new Map(commands.map((c) => [c.id, c]));\n352:   const problems = [];\n353:   const warnings = [];\n354:   const claimedNamespaces = new Set();\n355:   const declared = new Set();\n356: \n357:   entries.forEach((entry, index) => {\n358:     // A null or scalar entry carries no command to check; it is still drift,\n359:     // because the file no longer has the shape the advisor reads.\n360:     if (!isPlainObject(entry)) {\n361:       problems.push(`entry ${index + 1} is not an object`);\n362:       return;\n363:     }\n364:     const id = typeof entry.command === 'string' ? entry.command : '(unnamed entry)';\n365:     if (!COMMAND_ID_RE.test(id)) {\n366:       problems.push(`${id} is not a slash-command id`);\n367:       return;\n368:     }\n369:     declared.add(id);\n370:     const command = byId.get(id);\n371:     if (!command) {\n372:       problems.push(`${id} has an entry but no command file`);\n373:       return;\n374:     }\n375:     if (command.ns) claimedNamespaces.add(command.ns);\n376:     checkEntry(entry, command, repo, problems, warnings);\n377:   });\n378: \n379:   // A hub that speaks for a namespace speaks for all of it. Half a namespace is\n380:   // how a newly added command goes unrouted while the file sits happily on disk.\n381:   for (const ns of claimedNamespaces) {\n382:     for (const command of commands.filter((c) => c.ns === ns)) {\n383:       if (!declared.has(command.id)) {\n384:         problems.push(`${command.id} has no entry, though this hub covers the rest of ${ns}/`);\n385:       }\n386:     }\n387:   }\n388: \n389:   return { problems, warnings, entries: entries.length };\n390: }\n391: \n392: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n393: // 7. REPORT\n394: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n395: \n396: function main() {\n397:   const opts = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));\n398:   const commandsDir = path.join(opts.root, '.skilled/commands');\n399:   if (!fs.existsSync(commandsDir)) fail(`commands directory not found: ${commandsDir}`);\n400: \n401:   const commands = readCommandTree(commandsDir);\n402:   if (commands.length === 0) fail(`no command files under ${commandsDir}`);\n403:   const namespaces = new Set(commands.map((c) => c.ns).filter(Boolean));\n404: \n405:   const drift = [];\n406:   const prose = [];\n407: \n408:   console.log('\\n/doctor command-catalog-mirror — read-only coverage check');\n409:   console.log(`canonical: .skilled/commands frontmatter (${commands.length} commands)\\n`);\n410: \n411:   const catalogs = findCatalogs(commandsDir, [...namespaces].sort());\n412:   if (catalogs.length === 0) {\n413:     drift.push('catalog: no README.txt index found under .skilled/commands');\n414:   }\n415:   for (const catalog of catalogs) {\n416:     const result = checkCatalog(catalog, commands, namespaces);\n417:     const mark = result.problems.length === 0 ? 'OK  ' : 'DRIFT';\n418:     const label = catalog.label.padEnd(LABEL_WIDTH);\n419:     console.log(`  ${mark} ${label} ${result.covered}/${result.total} listed`);\n420:     for (const p of result.problems) {\n421:       console.log(`         - ${p}`);\n422:       drift.push(`${catalog.label}: ${p}`);\n423:     }\n424:   }\n425: \n426:   for (const meta of findMetadataFiles(opts.root)) {\n427:     const result = checkMetadata(meta, commands, opts.root);\n428:     if (result.entries === 0 && result.problems.length === 0) continue;\n429:     const mark = result.problems.length === 0 ? 'OK  ' : 'DRIFT';\n430:     const noun = result.entries === 1 ? 'entry' : 'entries';\n431:     console.log(`  ${mark} ${meta.label.padEnd(LABEL_WIDTH)} ${result.entries} ${noun}`);\n432:     for (const p of result.problems) {\n433:       console.log(`         - ${p}`);\n434:       drift.push(`${meta.label}: ${p}`);\n435:     }\n436:     for (const w of result.warnings) {\n437:       console.log(`         ? ${w}`);\n438:       prose.push(`${meta.label}: ${w}`);\n439:     }\n440:   }\n441: \n442:   if (prose.length > 0 && !opts.strict) {\n443:     console.log(`\\n  ${prose.length} prose divergence(s) reported above; --strict fails on them.`);\n444:   }\n445: \n446:   const failing = opts.strict ? drift.length + prose.length : drift.length;\n447:   if (failing > 0) {\n448:     console.log(`\\nSTATUS=DRIFT command-catalog-mirror: ${failing} issue(s)`);\n449:     console.log('Repair: the command file\\'s frontmatter is the source. Update the index row, '\n450:       + 'the group row or count, or the hub metadata entry to match it — '\n451:       + 'never the other way round.\\n');\n452:     process.exit(1);\n453:   }\n454:   console.log('\\nSTATUS=OK command-catalog-mirror: '\n455:     + 'every catalog and hub metadata covers the command tree\\n');\n456:   process.exit(0);\n457: }\n458: \n459: // Any throw is the checker failing, never a drift verdict, so it must reach the\n460: // exit code the workflow maps to checker error rather than Node's default 1.\n461: try {\n462:   main();\n463: } catch (err) {\n464:   fail(`checker crashed: ${err && err.message ? err.message : String(err)}`);\n465: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582807632,"end":1794582807753}}}}
