{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582845819,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5791709002l0ridZEIaSHxF4","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827beffe2WRM5fapKnxmNx","messageID":"msg_1d57910ff001GAwPpZVJvLgNNy","type":"tool","id":"call_00_Z3AXCnNgWyN9cEh7LQny7015","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -P '/create:skill(?![-\\w])' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md .skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml .skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml .skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/create/README.txt .skilled/commands/README.txt .skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":".skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt:154:| Enhanced prompt should become a skill | `/create:skill` | Scaffold an OpenCode skill from the prompt |\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs:184:// another (/create:skill inside /create:skill-parent). Any of those lets a\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1:# /create:skill Presentation Contract\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:3:This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/create:skill`: startup questions, setup/status dashboards, operation display, and result templates. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:28:Restart with: @markdown /create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type]\n.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:7:# /create:skill Router\n.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:13:Route /create:skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:5:# Entrypoint: /create:skill\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:626:      action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:628:      action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:630:      action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:5:# Entrypoint: /create:skill\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:571:    action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:573:    action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:575:    action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57:| **skill** | `/create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto\\|:confirm]` | Unified skill workflow (full-create, full-update, reference-only, asset-only) |\n.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:88:├── skill.md                      # /create:skill command\n.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:119:The `--chained` flag on `/create:skill` doc-only operations indicates parent workflow handoff.\n.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:137:/create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:149:/create:skill my-skill reference-only debugging :confirm\n.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:178:**Q: What does the `--chained` flag do on `/create:skill`?**\n.skilled/commands/README.txt:123:| Skill | `/create:skill <name> <operation> [type]` | Unified skill create/update/reference/asset workflow |\n.skilled/commands/README.txt:214:/create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":