h-human-voice.md           # /create:with-human-voice command\n └── assets/                       # One auto YAML, one confirm YAML and one presentation\n@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ Each mode loads a separate YAML workflow from `assets/` when that command ships\n - Auto: `create-<command>-auto.yaml`\n - Confirm: `create-<command>-confirm.yaml`\n \n-The `--chained` flag on `/create:skill` doc-only operations indicates parent workflow handoff.\n+The `--chained` flag on `/create:sk-skill` doc-only operations indicates parent workflow handoff.\n \n The documentation-package commands preserve the live `sk-doc` contracts:\n - `/create:feature-catalog` produces `feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md` plus bare descriptive-slug category folders (the root catalog owns display order)\n@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@ The documentation-package commands preserve the live `sk-doc` contracts:\n /create:readme readme .skilled/skills/my-skill --type skill :confirm\n \n # Create a full skill\n-/create:skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n+/create:sk-skill my-new-skill full-create :auto\n \n # Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets\n /create:skill-parent my-loop-workflows create --modes research,review,ai-council :confirm\n@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@ The documentation-package commands preserve the live `sk-doc` contracts:\n /create:manual-testing-playbook system-spec-kit update :auto\n \n # Add a reference doc to an existing skill\n-/create:skill my-skill reference-only debugging :confirm\n+/create:sk-skill my-skill reference-only debugging :confirm\n \n # Create a changelog from a completed spec folder\n /create:changelog specs/my-track/042-memory-upgrade :auto\n@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ The documentation-package commands preserve the live `sk-doc` contracts:\n \n A: Use `create` when the package folder does not yet exist under the skill root. Use `update` when the package already exists and you want to add or revise content within it. Running `create` on an existing package will produce a conflict error.\n \n-**Q: What does the `--chained` flag do on `/create:skill`?**\n+**Q: What does the `--chained` flag do on `/create:sk-skill`?**\n \n A: The `--chained` flag signals that the command was dispatched from a parent workflow (for example, a `full-create` that hands off to a doc-only phase). It changes how the command reports completion and does not affect the output files. Remove it when running the command standalone.\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml b/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml\nindex d20b6e5ef5..62c98fba8a 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n # OPENCODE CREATE: SK-SKILL UNIFIED WORKFLOW (AUTO MODE)\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n # Mode: autonomous execution (no approval checkpoints)\n-# Entrypoint: /create:skill\n+# Entrypoint: /create:sk-skill\n # Operations: full-create | full-update | reference-only | asset-only\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n \n@@ -568,11 +568,11 @@ termination:\n   message: \"Unified sk-skill auto workflow complete.\"\n   next_steps:\n   - condition: \"Need iterative updates\"\n-    action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n+    action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n   - condition: \"Need another reference\"\n-    action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n+    action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n   - condition: \"Need another asset\"\n-    action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n+    action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n \n rules:\n   ALWAYS:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml b/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml\nindex 32bdd2e94a..9736721d8a 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n # OPENCODE CREATE: SK-SKILL UNIFIED WORKFLOW (CONFIRM MODE)\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n # Mode: interactive execution with explicit checkpoints\n-# Entrypoint: /create:skill\n+# Entrypoint: /create:sk-skill\n # Operations: full-create | full-update | reference-only | asset-only\n # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n \n@@ -623,11 +623,11 @@ termination:\n   message: \"Unified sk-skill confirm workflow complete.\"\n   next_steps:\n     - condition: \"Need iterative updates\"\n-      action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n+      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n     - condition: \"Need another reference\"\n-      action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n+      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n     - condition: \"Need another asset\"\n-      action: \"/create:skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n+      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n \n rules:\n   ALWAYS:\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt\nindex 877fd153cd..80719e1174 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n-# /create:skill Presentation Contract\n+# /create:sk-skill Presentation Contract\n \n-This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/create:skill`: startup questions, setup/status dashboards, operation display, and result templates. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n+This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/create:sk-skill`: startup questions, setup/status dashboards, operation display, and result templates. The command router owns asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n \n ## 1. Phase 0 Verification Display\n \n@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ Hard-block message:\n \n ```text\n This command requires @markdown for template-first generation and sk-doc validation.\n-Restart with: @markdown /create:skill <skill-name> [operation] [type]\n+Restart with: @markdown /create:sk-skill <skill-name> [operation] [type]\n \n STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"Markdown agent required\"\n ```\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md b/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\nindex 7488b0f9db..afb8bcbdfa 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\n@@ -4,13 +4,13 @@ argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:aut\n allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n ---\n \n-# /create:skill Router\n+# /create:sk-skill Router\n \n This command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n \n ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n \n-Route /create:skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n+Route /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n \n - Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n - Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs b/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\nindex e51cfcc4ef..81ab5ce1e9 100755\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\n@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ function readCommandTree(commandsDir) {\n // Coverage is judged per table row, never over the whole document and never by\n // substring. A usage example further down mentions ids in passing, a group row's\n // description names the commands of its group, and one id can be the prefix of\n-// another (/create:skill inside /create:skill-parent). Any of those lets a\n+// another (/group:name inside /group:name-parent). Any of those lets a\n // deleted row hide, which is precisely the staleness worth catching. So a row\n // names the command its first backticked span opens with, compared exactly.\n //\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt b/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt\nindex 23402bbd88..44b595b7b5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt\n@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@ Standard failure messages:\n \n | Condition | Suggested Command | Reason |\n |-----------|-------------------|--------|\n-| Enhanced prompt should become a skill | `/create:skill` | Scaffold an OpenCode skill from the prompt |\n+| Enhanced prompt should become a skill | `/create:sk-skill` | Scaffold an OpenCode skill from the prompt |\n | Prompt-engineering patterns worth documenting | `/create:readme` | Package the results as a documentation artifact |\n \n End interactive presentations with a single next-step prompt.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md .skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml .skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml .skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt .skilled/commands/create/README.txt .skilled/commands/README.txt .skilled/commands/prompt/assets/prompt_improve_presentation.txt .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/command-catalog-mirror-check.cjs\", \"workdir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/pu